PVD("thailand_budget_2022",{"docs":["","Table I-4 Budget Allocation Strategy and Programme FY 2022"],"s":{"1":[[1,"","1.1","Strategic programme on strengthening the nation's principal institutions","5924.3 million baht · The amount will be allocated to instill everyone in the nation a conscience to cherish and treasure, maintain loyalty and uphold the nation's principal institutions. This can be done by protecting, maintaining and upholding the monarchy, providing safety to the monarchy and the royal family, mobilizing area development along the royal initiatives and the Philosophy of Sufficiency Economy, as well as giving support to the royal special activities.",""]],"2":[[1,"","1.2","Strategic programme on maintaining internal peace","21590.3 million baht · The amount will be allocating to create security and safety in life and belongings for the people by maintaining internal peace and domestic security. Emphasis will be made on cultivating a conscience and awareness on unity and promoting solidarity of people in the nation.",""]],"3":[[1,"","1.3","Strategic programme on developing and strengthening politics in the democratic regime with the monarchy as head of state","216.7 million baht · The amount will be allocated to create a higher level of political stability and governance by promoting public relations to develop politics and government under the democratic regime. People's engagement in politics, to create knowledge, understanding, faith and awareness as a good citizen under the democratic regime with the monarchy as head of state will be promoted.",""]],"4":[[1,"","1.4","Integrated programme on mobilization of problem rectification of southern border provinces","6912.1 million baht · The amount will be allocated to support the integrated efforts in protecting and solving the violence in the southern border provinces on a systematic and solidified approach. Public participation will be promoted to create understanding among the people both within and outside of the southern border provinces.",""]],"5":[[1,"","1.5","Strategic programme on management of problems of alien workforce and human trafficking","292.2 million baht · The amount will be allocated to enable the victims of human trafficking, child labour, forced labour and vulnerable groups to be systematically protected by providing the target groups with knowledge and understanding on the problems of human trafficking and capability to protect themselves from the said activities. Victims of human trafficking will be protected and welcome back to the society.",""]],"6":[[1,"","1.6","Integrated programme on prevention, suppression and treatment of drug addiction","4261.7 million baht · The amount will be allocated to create immunity from narcotics for children, youth, workforce and vulnerable groups and for them to avoid getting involved with drugs by organizing mechanisms to systematically prevent, solve the problems and assist people. Emphasis will be given to suppression and apprehension of drug producers and traffickers, influential people and every public official involved in the drug business.",""]],"7":[[1,"","1.7","Strategic programme on preventing and rectifying problems with repercussions to the security","14082.8 million baht · The amount will be allocated to address the existing security problems for lasting solutions to the extent that there will be no further effects to the administration and development of the country. This can be achieved by developing an internal security maintenance and country development plan, preventing transnational threats and marine security, preventing and solving cyber security problems, and terrorisms.",""]],"8":[[1,"","1.8","Strategic programme on developing national preparedness system and disaster management system","18267.6 million baht · The amount will be allocated to improve reliability of emergency and rescue operations, as well as to minimize loss, and ensure safety in people's life and property. Effort will be made on improving operational capability and providing knowledge and awareness in order to be prepared in dealing with disaster management and improving efficiency.",""]],"9":[[1,"","1.9","Strategic programme on developing potentials in national defence and preparedness in coping with all forms of threats","60181.3 million baht · The amount will be allocated to prepare the armed forces and national security agencies in coping with all forms of threats at every dimenstion and every degree of severity. National preparedness system and plan will be developed to be modernized and deployable.",""]],"10":[[1,"","1.10","Strategic programme on development of mechanisms for security administration on a holistic approach","252.7 million baht · The amount will be allocated to increase efficiency of security administrative mechanism. This will be done by promoting integration of security administrative mechanisms, enhancing preparedness and elevating security mechanism among agencies.",""]],"11":[[1,"","1.11","Strategic programme on promoting international relations","4049.5 million baht · The amount will be allocated to enable Thailand to have security and ability to cope with all forms of external challenges. This will also allows Thailand to become a sustainable development partner with other countries, and to be developed in harmony with international standards in every dimension.",""]],"12":[[1,"","1.12","Strategic programme on supporting national security","331.6 million baht · The amount will be allocated to support strategic goals on security by enhancing capability of the administrative system, maintaining the country's cyber security, mobilizing protection and problem solving in accordance with the transpiring situtations in the localities.",""]],"13":[[1,"","1.13","Fundamental programme on national security","52752.3 million baht · The amount will be allocated to ensure efficient and cost effective administration of the missions on security and enabling public agencies to consistently perform and provide services according to the standard, authority and legal framework. It also covers taking good care of personnel, workplaces, equipments and working environment.",""]],"14":[[1,"","1.14","Programme on public sector personnel","194683.3 million baht · The amount will be allocated to ensure efficiency and cost effectiveness in the management of public sector personnel with regard to the government's operations. It also supports the development of work systems and improvement of personnel's competency in performing their duties with integrity and ethics while maintaining their work-life balance.",""]],"15":[[1,"","2.1","Strategic programme on value creation agriculture","45542.2 million baht · The amount will be allocated to enable expansion of the agricultural sector in the Gross Domestic Product, an increase in agricultural productivity and capability in processing products into high-value ones through value creation of agricultural products based on their potentials and uniquenesses. Technology will be applied to develop robust and sustainable agricultural resource bases.",""]],"16":[[1,"","2.2","Integrated programme on development of future industries and services","856.6 million baht · The amount will be allocated to increase growth rate of the manufacturing sector in the Gross Domestic Product and increase manufacturing and service productivity throughout the supply chain. This can be achieved by promoting the food of the future industry on an integrated basis and creating the bio-industry economy, developing the medical services industry, promoting research and development and creating innovation.",""]],"17":[[1,"","2.3","Integrated programme on creating income from tourism","4574.5 million baht · The amount will be allocated to enable tourism as a mechanism in mobilizing the country's economy. The goal is to increase revenues from tourism which consequently increase its proportion in the total Gross Domestic Product by promoting domestic tourism, distributing tourism activities in term of areas and income to the communities as well as giving priority to the development of sustainable tourism.",""]],"18":[[1,"","2.4","Strategic programme on area development and smart livable city","6805.5 million baht · The amount will be allocated to improve Thailand's competitiveness by creating centers of economic and social prosperity in every region of the country and developing infrastructure for transportation, communication and energy systems with modern digital technologies. Economic and social prosperity will be distributed to elevate the cities' livability.",""]],"19":[[1,"","2.5","Integrated programme on development of transport and logistic system","107481.0 million baht · The amount will be allocated for development of transport infrastructure and logistic system with comprehensive connectivity covering domestic and international routes leading to the enhancement of the country's competitiveness. Multimodal transport will be promoted in order to reduce logistic costs and increase the country's competitiveness.",""]],"20":[[1,"","2.6","Strategic programe on development of energy security","1139.3 million baht · The amount will be allocated to enable Thailand to have energy security and improve efficiency in the country's energy consumption. This can be achieved by promoting energy exploration, supporting development of energy infrastructure at an appropriate level, maintaining domestic production of crude oil and liquefied natural gas, diversifying appropriate types of energy and creating a system to cope with energy emergency situations.",""]],"21":[[1,"","2.7","Strategic programme on development of digital economy and society","1719.9 million baht · The amount will be allocated to increase economic value of digital businesses utilizing digital technology. This will be done through developing digital infrastructure with emphasis on the thorough internet coverage, elevating digital community and online learning centers, enabling people an access to data and services, promoting investment and utilization of common digital infrastructure resources.",""]],"22":[[1,"","2.8","Integrated programme on development of business operators and small and medium-sized enterprises","1867.9 million baht · The amount will be allocated to enable operators of small and medium-sized enterprises and community operators to have knowledge and skills for being entrepreneurs, ability to compete and possess innovation on creating business models, manufacturing process and service provision as well as digital and information technology skills and an access to domestic and international markets. Moreover, support will be given to capital acquisition which satisfies different operator's requirements and the expansion of trade and investment.",""]],"23":[[1,"","2.9","Strategic programme on development of special economic zones","655.3 million baht · The amount will be allocated to develop the special economic zones as the centers of economic and social prosperity by providing infrastructure on communication, social, environment and education to the area, increasing efficiency of customs checkpoints and making proposals on new laws and regulations. Attention will be given to public relations focusing on both, Thai and international investors, to invest in the target areas.",""]],"24":[[1,"","2.10","Integrated programme on development of the Eastern Economic Corridor","11944.8 million baht · The amount will be allocated to promote modern and environmental-friendly economic activities, increase the country's competitiveness, develop efficient infrastructure and public utility system with continuity, accessibility, comprehensive and systematic connectivity. Emphasis will be made on development of attractive and livable cities with international modernity.",""]],"25":[[1,"","2.11","Strategic programme on innovation research and development","14207.4 million baht · The amount will be allocated to promote, support and mobilize the country's research and innovation system to create and support application of research and innovation findings for economic and social benefits leading to a balanced and sustainable development of the country. This will be achieved by encouraging both the public and private sectors to use research and innovation findings with emphasis on those being responsive to the country's needs.",""]],"26":[[1,"","2.12","Strategic programme on development of science, technology and innovation potentials","445.6 million baht · The amount will be allocated to enable Thailand's development toward the society founded upon the knowledge-based economy. This can be achieved by developing infrastructure and amenities on science and modern technology, standards of quality system, and testing analysis accredited under the international agreements and in accordance with the current and future industry requirements.",""]],"27":[[1,"","2.13","Strategic programme on supporting the development of competitiveness","19989.5 million baht · The amount will be allocated to enable Thailand to achieve stable and sustainable economic growth by elevating the country's diverse potentials in the economy, identity, culture, tradition, way of life and natural resources as well as the country's other comparative advantages together with technology and innovation to be in harmony with the economic and social contexts of the modern world society. Emphasis will be given to the development of the country's various infrastructures.",""]],"28":[[1,"","2.14","Fundamental programme on the development of competitiveness","72986.3 million baht · The amount will be allocated to enable the efficiency and cost effectiveness in implementation of the country's competitiveness development allowing government agencies to operate and provide services on a continued basis with standard. Transport systems connecting infrastructure and amenities within the cities and regions and quality of public transport and traffic will be improved.",""]],"29":[[1,"","2.15","Programme on public sector personnel","41917.8 million baht · The amount will be allocated to ensure efficiency and cost effectiveness in the management of public sector personnel with regard to the government's operations along with the development of the work systems of government agencies. It also improves personnel's competency in performing their duties with integrity and ethics while maintaining their work-life balance.",""]],"30":[[1,"","3.1","Strategic programme on realignment of value and culture","1763.7 million baht · The amount will be allocated to enable Thai people to be of morality, value, respectable value with public conscience, responsibility to the society with patriotism and taking pride on the nation, religions and monarchy and adopting the Philosophy of Sufficiency Economy in daily life. In addition, communities and conservation of localities will be encouraged to promote and disseminate, develop and inherit arts and cultural heritage, local wisdom.",""]],"31":[[1,"","3.2","Strategic programme on development of human potentials on a life-long basis","6088.4 million baht · The amount will be allocated to enable Thai people of every age group to have physically, mentally, morally and the surroundings enhanced in terms of potentials which will contribute to security in life through promotion and development of children from infancy to early childhood for the age-based development with quality. Attention will be given to promote education and lifelong learning with quality, standard and necessary skills to accommodate living in the 21st century.",""]],"32":[[1,"","3.3","Strategic programme on development of education and learning quality","12225.3 million baht · The amount will be allocated to provide students, teachers, education personnel and the public to attain quality education conformed to national education standards by strengthening and developing learning systems responsive to every dimension of change and every age group in the 21st century. Emphasis will be made to a newly designed learning system, development of media and digital technologies, promotion of production and quality improvement of teachers and education personnel.",""]],"33":[[1,"","3.4","Strategic programme on good public health promotion","51978.5 million baht · The amount will be allocated to enable people to attain good health and have access to a standard public health system by promoting the public health system reform emphasizing promotion of a thorough medical system, providing family doctors and Tambon health promotion hospitals. These measures will allow people in the communities to take care of their own health and the communities can be self-reliant on healthcare with sustainability.",""]],"34":[[1,"","3.5","Strategic programme on enhancing sports potentials","1748.9 million baht · The amount will be allocated to enable Thai people to have good health by encouraging people to gain knowledge and realize the importance of excercising and participating in basic sports which are essential as living skills. It also promotes participation in exercise, sports and recreational activities among people of every age group and supports development of infrastructure, equipment and facilities.",""]],"35":[[1,"","3.6","Strategic programme on supporting human potentials development and reinforcement","4750.3 million baht · The amount will be allocated to support the strategic goal on developing and enhancing human resource potentials enabling Thai people to be decent, smart and be prepared for the 21st century with supportive environment for a life-long human development. Emphasis will be made on development of people in every dimension and age group to be decent and capable with quality.",""]],"36":[[1,"","3.7","Fundamental programme on human potentials development and reinforcement","58730.3 million baht · The amount will be allocated to carry out responsibilities to develop and strengthen human potentials with efficiency and cost effectiveness. It will allow public agencies to operate and provide standard services on a continuous basis in accordance with the laws.",""]],"37":[[1,"","3.8","Programme on public sector personnel","408283.0 million baht · The amount will be allocated to ensure efficiency and cost effectiveness in the management of public sector personnel with regard to the government's operation along with the development of the work systems of government agencies. It also improves personnel's competency in performing their duties with integrity and ethics while maintaining their work-life balance.",""]],"38":[[1,"","4.1","Strategic programme on social empowerment","7442.1 million baht · The amount will be allocated to encourage every segment to increase its engagement in strengthening the society by promoting the community empowerment in becoming the social force. This will be achieved by supporting role and potential development of social welfare organizations, volunteers, networks and the civic sector, strengthening robustness of the disabillities groups and networks.",""]],"39":[[1,"","4.2","Strategic programme on decentralization to the Local Administrative Organizations","294667.3 million baht · The amount will be allocated to be in harmony with the Determining Plans and Process of Decentralization to Local Government Organization Act B.E. 2542 and its amendments requiring an increase in decentralization and enabling people to receive efficient public services from the Local Administrative Organanizations. Implementation will be on important tasks including basic education, supplementary food and lunches, and allowances to the elderly and persons with disabilities.",""]],"40":[[1,"","4.3","Strategic programme on promoting integrated development of provinces and clusters of provinces","17411.0 million baht · The amount will be allocated to support integrated operations covering every dimension of the development of provinces and clusters of provinces in accordance with the direction of the national development by giving priorities to the public participation process to meet the needs and solve local problems. This will connect strategies on the country's development toward the mobilization at the local level covering every dimension.",""]],"41":[[1,"","4.4","Integrated programme on preparedness to accommodate the aging society","617.6 million baht · The amount will be allocated to encourage population from 25 to 59 years of age to be prepared on every dimension by promoting awareness prior to entering the aging society. Priorities will be given to the public relations campaign providing data, news; development of network mechanism to create knowledge and skills in order to be prepared for the aging society.",""]],"42":[[1,"","4.5","Integrated programme on development and promotion of local economy","1506.4 million baht · The amount will be allocated to enable people to attain higher income, reduce proverty and be able to manage debts with efficiency, develop new generation of farmers to become smart ones, elevate potentials of entrepreneurs by enhancing potentials of the target groups of people to have access to sources of capital and land for living. Attention will be given to promotion and development of occupations by preparing a career development plan at the tambon level.",""]],"43":[[1,"","4.6","Strategic programme on creating social security","281496.8 million baht · The amount will be allocated to enable people, especially the underprivileged and vulnerable groups to be protected and attain appropriate and fair social security and welfare with accessibility to medical and public health service under the universal health care system with thoroughness and quality. Moreover, additional benefits will be given to the case of liver transplant and health care services from family physicians at the primary health care facilities.",""]],"44":[[1,"","4.7","Strategic programme on creating equality in education","82214.0 million baht · The amount will be allocated to create opportunities to access quality and standard education on a thorough basis, and to receive basic education on both formal and informal systems according to the stipulated right. These can be achieved by providing financial support for education from kindergarten to the completion of basic education, consisting of tuition fees, books and amenities, student uniforms and learners' quality development activity fees.",""]],"45":[[1,"","4.8","Strategic programme on targeted measures to solve group-specific problems","3237.6 million baht · The amount will be allocated to provide a system and mechanism to target groups who need specific assistances and additional coverage by developing systems and mechanisms for assistance. Appropriate infrastructure will be supported and provided for various groups of people, especially children, youths, women, people with disabilities, the elderly and the socially under privileged.",""]],"46":[[1,"","4.9","Strategic programme on supporting creation of social opportunities and equality","32097.4 million baht · The amount will be allocated to elevate quality of life of low income people and farmers by providing welfare along the Pracharat guideline through the public welfare card enabling improved quality of life, accessibility to basic necessities in life as well as promoting savings as assurance for payments of pensions and benefits to members at the end of membership through the National Savings Fund. Members of co-operatives and farmers groups will be provided with a relief on debts.",""]],"47":[[1,"","4.10","Fundamental programme on creating of social opportunities and equality","2567.7 million baht · The amount will be allocated to support the strategy on creating social opportunities and equality, enabling people to attain opportunities in accessing public services on an equitable, fair and thorough basis; to strengthen the family with warmth and immunity toward good quality of life. People will be encouraged to engage in the development of community council which is a mechanism to strengthen the local communities.",""]],"48":[[1,"","4.11","Programme on public sector personnel","8449.5 million baht · The amount will be allocated to ensure efficiency and cost effectiveness in the management of public sector personnel with regard to the government's operations along with the development of the work systems of government agencies. It also improves personnel's competency in performing their duties with integrity and ethics while maintaining their work-life balance.",""]],"49":[[1,"","5.1","Strategic programme on creation of sustainable growth with regard to conservation, rehabilitation and prevention of natural resources destruction","3951.1 million baht · The amount will be allocated to conserve and rehabilitate bio-diversity by developing mechanisms and measures in conserving, preventing, protecting, rehabilitating and using the bio-diversity with sustainability. Appropriate utilizing of water source areas, cultivation of economic woods and comprehensive industries will also be promoted.",""]],"50":[[1,"","5.2","Strategic programme on creation of sustainable growth of marine economic society","383.4 million baht · The amount will be allocated to improve, rehabilitate and renew marine and coastal resources by developing and increasing the proportion of eco-friendly marine activities. Marine bio-economic values will be increased, coral and sea grass will be rehabilitated while the eco-system, and rare or near-extinct marine creatures will be conserved.",""]],"51":[[1,"","5.3","Strategic programme on coping with repercussions from climate change","1108.8 million baht · The amount will be allocated to enable the country to reduce the emission of greenhouse gases and lessen repercussions from natural disasters and climate change. Emphasis will be made on initiating co-operations among various members and strengthening capability in reducing industrial pollutants to support the measures on reducing green house gases from manufacturing plants.",""]],"52":[[1,"","5.4","Strategic programme on dealing with pollution and the environment","267.0 million baht · The amount will be allocated to enable efficient and quality management of the environment conducive to good quality of life of the people by implementing systematic waste and refuse management, dealing with toxic waste at originating sources and managing air quality of each locality to be within the standard. Emphasis will be made on development of tools and mechanisms in preventing and reducing pollution.",""]],"53":[[1,"","5.5","Strategic programme on elevating paradigms to stipulate the country's natural resources and environment","79.2 million baht · The amount will be allocated to enable Thai people to have desirable character and behaviour with regard to the environment and well-being by promoting development and elevation of an environmental assessment at the strategy level. There will be pressing for arrangement of a structure to mobilize issues on co-management of natural resources and environment at the country and international levels.",""]],"54":[[1,"","5.6","Integrated programme on management of water resources","63136.4 million baht · The amount will be allocated to enable the country to increase water security, have systematic and sustainable water resource management, increase a balance of usable water stock, and improve water productivity consumption. In doing so, water for consumption, agriculture, manufacturing and industry will be managed.",""]],"55":[[1,"","5.7","Strategic programme on supporting creation of growth on the environmental-friendly quality of life","21870.9 million baht · The amount will be allocated to conserve, maintain and utilize natural resources and the environment on a balanced and sustainable basis, elevate nature-based tourist attractions, promote water sources for the operations of the Royal Initiated Projects and promote the management of water for irrigation and the land realignment for irrigation.",""]],"56":[[1,"","5.8","Fundamental programme on creation of growth on the environmental-friendly quality of life","9845.8 million baht · The amount will be allocated for the operations on natural resources and the environment, protection of conserved forest areas, national reserved forests for fertility, promotion of water management, provision of support to the entire artificial precipitation operations, development of learning sources and plant strain conservation, and creating security for mineral resource base.",""]],"57":[[1,"","5.9","Programme on public sector personnel","18464.9 million baht · The amount will be allocated to ensure efficiency and cost effectiveness in the management of public sector personnel with regard to the government's operations along with the development of the work systems of government agencies. It also improves personnel's competency in performing their duties with integrity and ethics while maintaining their work-life balance.",""]],"58":[[1,"","6.1","Strategic programme on improvement of public service delivery and the public sector's efficiency","22931.9 million baht · The amount will be allocated to improve public service delivery enabling ease, convenience, promptness, transparency, cost reduction and verifiability as well as monetary and fiscal management by improving efficiency of revenue collection, expanding tax base, and improving the taxation system suitable for the country's economic situation. Attention will be given to development of a medium and long-term fiscal system and improvement of the budgeting process.",""]],"59":[[1,"","6.2","Integrated programme on digital government","2409.4 million baht · The amount will be allocated to develop a model to deliver the public sector's services by adopting digital technology and putting people at the center. This will be supported by developing the public sector's service of worthiness and implementation at the international standard with promptness, ease, efficiency, transparency and verifiability through cost reduction and lessening steps of operations.",""]],"60":[[1,"","6.3","Integrated programme on anti-corruption and misconduct","478.9 million baht · The amount will be allocated to reduce corruption in the Thai society through instilling of conscience and creating values for every segment to be aware of integrity, morality, virtue and adopting the governance principle on organizational management. Emphasis will be made on revision of laws and strict and fair enforcement as well as allowing people to engage in preventing, suppressing corruption and misconduct.",""]],"61":[[1,"","6.4","Strategic programme on developing laws and the judicial process","2988.1 million baht · The amount will be allocated to develop laws applicable to different contexts to be in harmony with changes and development as well as enforcement of laws with transparency and efficiency. Judicial process will be promoted and managed for impartiality, equity and fairness in the society.",""]],"62":[[1,"","6.5","Strategic programme on supporting realignment for balance and development of administrative system of the public sector","1928.7 million baht · The amount will be allocated to support the strategic goal on realigning and developing the public administrative system that is for the public sector to have the work culture emphasizing the results and benefits for the general public, addressing people's needs with ease, promptness, transparency at a reduced size, agility for change, and absence of corruption and misconduct for the country's public benefits. Emphasis will be made on adopting and applying Big Data innovation technology and digital work process.",""]],"63":[[1,"","6.6","Fundamental programme on realignment for balance and development of administrative system of the public sector","429517.6 million baht · The amount will be allocated to carry out responsibilities on realigning and developing an administrative system to be efficient and cost effectiveness allowing public agencies to operate and provide standard services on a continuous basis and in accordance with the laws. It also maintains personnel, places of work, equipment and the working environment in good condition.",""]],"64":[[1,"","6.7","Programme on public sector personnel","98361.4 million baht · The amount will be allocated to ensure efficiency and cost effectiveness in the management of public sector personnel with regard to the government's operations along with the development of the work systems of government agencies. It also improves personnel's competency in performing their duties with integrity and ethics while maintaining their work-life balance.",""]],"65":[[1,"","7.1","Programme on attending to emergencies or necessities","105862.0 million baht · The amount will be allocated as reserves for expenditures to prevent or rectify problems detrimental to people's peace, and the state's security, to remedy or mitigate damages from public disasters and to be used for the state's urgent necessities with respect to the fiscal discipline.",""]],"66":[[1,"","7.2","Programme on management of public debt","297631.4 million baht · The amount will be allocated to support the efficient management and repayment of public debt with maximum benefits to the economy.",""]],"67":[[1,"","7.3","Programme on expenditures for replenishment of treasury account balance","596.7 million baht · The amount will be allocated to reimburse expenditures which have already been made from the treasury account in accordance with the Treasury Account Act of B.E. 2491 and its amendments.",""]],"68":[[1,"","7.4","Programme on expenditures for replenishment of reserve fund","24978.6 million baht · The amount will be allocated to reimburse the fund used for spendings in the event of necessities and emergencies for the country's benefits where the Contingency Fund for Emergencies or Immediate Needs in the Central Fund was insufficient and the reserved fund has been used in accordance with section 45 of the Budget Procedure Act B.E. 2561.",""]]}});
PVD("thailand_budget_2023",{"docs":["","Table I-4 Budget Allocation Strategy and Program FY 2023"],"s":{"1":[[1,"","1.1","Strategic Program on Strengthening the Nation's Principal Institutions","12259.9 million baht · The budget will be used to instill everyone in the nation a conscience to cherish and treasure, maintain loyalty and uphold the nation's principal institutions. This includes protecting, maintaining and upholding the monarchy, providing safety to the monarchy and the royal family, honoring core institutions and strengthening national identity, mobilizing area development along the royal initiatives and the Sufficiency Economy Philosophy, as well as giving support to the royal special activities.",""]],"2":[[1,"","1.2","Strategic Program on Maintaining Internal Peace","22117.4 million baht · The budget will be used to create security and safety in the citizens' lives and properties by maintaining internal peace and domestic security. Emphasis will be made on cultivating a conscience and awareness on unity, promoting solidarity of people in the nation, supporting the mission of the Territorial Defense Volunteers and Local Militias, strengthening crime prevention and suppression, enforcing laws, providing justice and services to the people, as well as creating public participation among all sectors.",""]],"3":[[1,"","1.3","Strategic Program on Developing and Strengthening Politics in the Democratic Regime with the Monarchy as Head of State","531.2 million baht · The budget will be used to create political stability and good governance by promoting public relations to develop democracy, promoting public participation, and creating knowledge, understanding, and awareness of the good citizenship under the democratic regime with the monarchy as head of state.",""]],"4":[[1,"","1.4","Integrated Program on Mobilization of Problem Rectification of Southern Border Provinces","6251.2 million baht · The budget will be used to create national security, and safety in the citizens' lives and properties so that the people in the area are able to live together peacefully in a multicultural society. Support will be given to solve the problems and develop the southern border provinces by using an integrated system and unity covering all areas and target groups, including improving intelligence operations, creating understanding among the people, providing justice and remedying the victims, preventing illegal activities, and developing area potential in agriculture, infrastructure, and vocational and labor skills.",""]],"5":[[1,"","1.5","Strategic Program on Management of Problems of Alien Workforce and Human Trafficking","299.7 million baht · The budget will be used to mobilize operations in the prevention of forced labor and human trafficking, and enable the victims of human trafficking, child labor, fishing labor, forced labor and risk groups to be systematically protected. Alien workforce will be provided with legitimate documents, cooperating networks will be created, and workplaces, risk groups, and labor will be inspected and protected from human trafficking while legal actions against cases are enhanced.",""]],"6":[[1,"","1.6","Integrated Program on Prevention, Suppression and Treatment of Drug Addiction","4188.2 million baht · The budget will be used to create immunity from narcotics for children, youth, workforce and risk groups, and for them to avoid getting involved with drugs. Emphasis will be given to organizing mechanisms to systematically prevent and solve the problems, suppress and arrest drug producers and traffickers, and provide treatment and rehabilitation to drug addicts through a systematic assistance and treatment system.",""]],"7":[[1,"","1.7","Strategic Program on Preventing and Rectifying Problems with Repercussions to the Security","19919.6 million baht · The budget will be used to address existing security problems for lasting solutions so that there will be no further effects to the administration and development of the country. This includes maintaining internal, border, and coastal security, safeguarding national marine interests, preventing and solving cyber security problems and terrorism, preventing transnational threats and maritime security, and developing capacity to deal with nuclear and radiation threats and emergencies.",""]],"8":[[1,"","1.8","Strategic Program on Developing National Preparedness System and Disaster Management System","16971.8 million baht · The budget will be used to improve reliability of emergency and rescue operations, minimize loss, and ensure safety in the citizens' lives and properties. Efforts will be made on improving operational capacity, providing equipment for disaster prevention and recovery, increasing disaster warning efficiency, training staff, and providing knowledge and awareness to the public.",""]],"9":[[1,"","1.9","Strategic Program on Developing National Defence Capacity and Preparedness in Coping with all Forms of Threats","58194.4 million baht · The budget will be used to prepare national security agencies to cope with all forms of threats. Attention will be made on increasing capacity of intelligence and anti-intelligence operations, enhancing the armed forces capacity in developing the country and assisting the people, and promoting and developing the national defense industry, military energy, along with research and development to support national defense.",""]],"10":[[1,"","1.10","Strategic Program on Developing a Holistic Security Administration Mechanism","423.1 million baht · The budget will be used to increase efficiency of security management mechanism by promoting a holistic security mechanism to mobilize the National Security Policy and Plan.",""]],"11":[[1,"","1.11","Strategic Program on Promoting International Relations","4052.4 million baht · The budget will be used to enable Thailand to have security and ability to cope with all forms of external challenges, and to become a sustainable development partner with other countries in harmony with international standards. It will improve standards, promote economic and military relations and cooperation, enhance Thailand's image and role in the global community, and develop cooperation in science, technology and innovation partnership under international cooperation frameworks.",""]],"12":[[1,"","1.12","Strategic Program on Supporting National Security","536.8 million baht · The budget will be used to support strategic goals on security by enhancing capacity of the national security management system, and supporting operations to prevent and solve problems from the situation in the southern border provinces.",""]],"13":[[1,"","1.13","Fundamental Program on National Security","33838.4 million baht · The budget will be used to ensure efficient and cost-effective administration of the national security missions, and enable government agencies to consistently perform and provide services according to their authorities, legal frameworks, and the set standard, as well as taking good care of personnel, workplaces, equipment and work environment.",""]],"14":[[1,"","1.14","Program on Public Sector Personnel","116419.5 million baht · The budget will be used to ensure efficiency and cost effectiveness in the management of public sector personnel. In addition, there will be development of the government agencies' work system and personnel capacity in order to perform their duties with efficiency, morality and ethics while maintaining their work-life balance.",""]],"15":[[1,"","2.1","Strategic Program on Value Creation Agriculture","78903.7 million baht · The budget will be used to enable expansion of the Gross Domestic Product in the agricultural sector, increase agricultural productivity and capability in processing products into high-value ones by using technology to develop a robust and sustainable agricultural resource base. Emphasis will be made on research and development, strengthening farmers' livelihood via Income Guarantee Scheme, improving production toward safety standards, promoting added value for agricultural products, and creating new generation of farmers and farmers integration.",""]],"16":[[1,"","2.2","Integrated Program on Development of Future Industries and Services","1554.6 million baht · The budget will be used to increase growth rate of the Gross Domestic Product in manufacturing and services sectors, and increase productivity throughout the supply chain. This can be achieved by promoting bio-industry, developing high-technology entrepreneurs and labor, promoting research and development and innovation, supporting the utilization of intellectual property, and upgrading industries to high-technology industries.",""]],"17":[[1,"","2.3","Integrated Program on Creating Income from Tourism","5125.1 million baht · The budget will be used to enable tourism as a mechanism in mobilizing the country's economy by increasing revenue from tourism and investment in industry and services in the tourism sector. Attention will be placed on distributing tourism activities and income, focusing on sustainable tourism development, developing the whole tourism system with a focus on quality tourists, preserving the country's uniqueness, improving infrastructure and facilities, and building confidence in tourism safety.",""]],"18":[[1,"","2.4","Strategic Program on Area Development and Smart Livable City","7435.2 million baht · The budget will be used to improve Thailand's competitiveness by creating centers of economic and social prosperity in every region and developing transportation, communication and energy infrastructure with modern digital technologies. Economic and social prosperity will be distributed to elevate cities' livability, with support for city development databases, facilities and safety.",""]],"19":[[1,"","2.5","Integrated Program on Development of Transport and Logistic System","131372.8 million baht · The budget will be used to provide Thailand with efficient transportation and logistic systems, and reduce logistic costs leading to an increase in the country's competitiveness. Road, waterways, rail, and air transportation infrastructures and amenities will be developed, along with public transportation, logistics and supply chain management systems, trade facilitation, customs procedures, and international logistics networks.",""]],"20":[[1,"","2.6","Strategic Program on Development of Energy Security","1226.1 million baht · The budget will be used to enable Thailand to have energy security and improve efficiency in the country's energy consumption. Emphasis will be made on promoting renewable and alternative energy, improving efficiency of energy consumption in every sector, providing and developing stable energy infrastructure, supervising the energy market mechanism, restructuring energy prices, and revising laws and regulations.",""]],"21":[[1,"","2.7","Strategic Program on Development of Digital Economy and Society","988.1 million baht · The budget will be used to increase value of digital businesses as a proportion of the Gross Domestic Product through developing digital infrastructure covering the main communication network and high-speed broadband network throughout the country. Attention will be placed on digital infrastructure, big data centers, privacy protection, personal data protection, cyber threat countermeasures, and providing people in every occupation with knowledge and skills on technology utilization.",""]],"22":[[1,"","2.8","Strategic Program on Supporting Strong and Competitive Small and Medium-sized Enterprises","2721.4 million baht · The budget will be used to encourage small and medium-sized enterprises and community entrepreneurs to have knowledge and skills of entrepreneurship with a clear identity, competitiveness and innovation. Supports will be given to the use of technology and innovation, financing, access to resources and knowledge, expansion of trade and investment, and adjustment of business models to meet market demand.",""]],"23":[[1,"","2.9","Strategic Program on Development of Special Economic Zones","699.4 million baht · The budget will be used to develop the special economic zones as the center of economic and social prosperity by providing infrastructure on communication, social, environment and education, increasing efficiency of customs checkpoints and making proposals on new laws and regulations. Focus will also be on immigration services, border public health, communicable disease control, labor skills, foreign workers system, and border area development using digital technology and innovation.",""]],"24":[[1,"","2.10","Integrated Program on Development of the Eastern Economic Corridor","11086.9 million baht · The budget will be used to promote investments in the Eastern Economic Corridor. Emphasis will be put on supporting modern and environmental-friendly economic activities, developing efficient and connected infrastructure and public utility systems, developing attractive and livable cities, strengthening Thailand's role as the gateway to the Asian region, elevating deep-water ports and multi-purpose piers, and developing personnel competency to meet entrepreneurs' needs.",""]],"25":[[1,"","2.11","Strategic Program on Innovation Research and Development","17089.0 million baht · The budget will be used to enable the public and private sectors to apply the practical results of research and innovation development for economic and social benefits with an emphasis on research that is responsive to the country's needs. Focus will be placed on encouraging private sector engagement, developing standards and analytic testing services, and using research and innovation to support workforce development, resource conservation, pollution management and greenhouse gas management.",""]],"26":[[1,"","2.12","Strategic Program on Development of Science, Technology and Innovation Potentials","286.6 million baht · The budget will be used to enable Thailand's development toward the society founded upon the knowledge-based economy. This can be achieved by developing infrastructure and amenities on science and modern technology, standards of quality system and testing analysis, and supporting technology transfer, research and development, engineering design, and process and product development through integration mechanisms between relevant agencies.",""]],"27":[[1,"","2.13","Strategic Program on Supporting Development of Competitiveness","23775.5 million baht · The budget will be used to support the strategic goal of developing the country's competitiveness to make Thailand a developed country with stable and sustainable economic growth. Emphasis will be given to elevating the country's potential in various dimensions, developing infrastructures, adjusting the environment to enhance entrepreneurs' potential, expanding trade and investment opportunities, and building income base and new employment.",""]],"28":[[1,"","2.14","Fundamental Program on Development of Competitiveness","71873.9 million baht · The budget will be used to enable efficiency and cost effectiveness in implementation of the country's competitiveness development allowing government agencies to operate and continuously provide quality public services. Attention will be placed on management of land and water resources, promoting trade, controlling product standards and prices, developing entrepreneurial potential, promoting marketing and tourism, maintaining transportation systems and amenities, and ensuring safe transport, travel and traffic.",""]],"29":[[1,"","2.15","Program on Public Sector Personnel","41987.2 million baht · The budget will be used to ensure efficiency and cost effectiveness in the management of public sector personnel. In addition, there will be development of the government agencies' work system and personnel capacity in order to perform their duties with efficiency, morality and ethics while maintaining their work-life balance.",""]],"30":[[1,"","3.1","Strategic Program on Realignment of Value and Culture","2472.3 million baht · The budget will be used to enable Thai people to be ethical, moral, proud and embrace Thainess. The budget will be used to conserve local culture and traditions, and the Sufficiency Economy Philosophy will be adopted in daily life in order to build a peaceful society and enhance Thai image to the international level.",""]],"31":[[1,"","3.2","Strategic Program on Development of Human Potentials on a Life-Long Basis","31699.5 million baht · The budget will be used with a goal to improve every Thai people's life physically, mentally, and morally. Children and youth will have growth and appropriate skill development according to their age, education and life-long learning will be promoted, skill development for pupils and labor will be supported, and the elderly will be prepared to be self-reliant.",""]],"32":[[1,"","3.3","Strategic Program on Development of Education and Learning Quality","19871.4 million baht · The budget will be used to provide Thai people with quality and standard education system. Learning process will be reformed with regard to innovation and changes in the 21st century, teachers and education personnel will be equipped with academic and class management skills, and opportunities for vocational education and skill training will be expanded.",""]],"33":[[1,"","3.4","Strategic Program on Good Public Health Promotion","51883.9 million baht · The budget will be used to provide people with good health, increase access to standard public health services, and prepare for the outbreak of emerging and re-emerging diseases. Actions include promoting Village Public Health Volunteer mechanism, promoting Thai herbs and traditional medicine, training new doctors, nurses, and public health personnel, developing emergency medical and referral systems, and adopting digital technology to support medical service.",""]],"34":[[1,"","3.5","Strategic Program on Enhancing Sports Potentials","1934.3 million baht · The budget will be used to ensure that Thai people will have good health. Emphasis will be made on promoting exercises, sports and recreational activities, cultivating sportsmanship and discipline, empowering national and youth athletes, developing sport and recreational personnel, and ensuring standard and quality sport science, infrastructure, equipment, and venues.",""]],"35":[[1,"","3.6","Strategic Program on Supporting Human Potentials Development and Reinforcement","2650.2 million baht · The budget will be used to support the Human Potential Development and Reinforcement Strategy by supporting Thai people to be good and ethical. The budget will be used to make sure that the citizen have development and good health and be prepared for life in the 21st century, upgrade education data systems, build new labor skills and advance current skills, and expand learning and career training opportunities across the country.",""]],"36":[[1,"","3.7","Fundamental Program on Human Potentials Development and Reinforcement","35057.3 million baht · The budget will be used to efficiently carry out missions and lawful power in human resource development. The budget will be used to ensure Thai people will be ethical and generous, support people potential development, improve the quality and accessibility of education and learning systems, and promote good health.",""]],"37":[[1,"","3.8","Program on Public Sector Personnel","403945.1 million baht · The budget will be used to ensure efficiency and cost effectiveness in the management of public sector personnel. In addition, there will be development of the government agencies' work system and personnel capacity in order to perform their duties with efficiency, morality and ethics while maintaining their work-life balance.",""]],"38":[[1,"","4.1","Strategic Program on Social Empowerment","7949.7 million baht · The budget will be used to encourage every segment in the society to be more participated in social development. This can be done by promoting community empowerment, supporting social welfare organizations, volunteers, networks, and civil society, strengthening local communities, providing places to live and arable land, and conserving and restoring local arts and cultures.",""]],"39":[[1,"","4.2","Strategic Program on Decentralization to the Local Administrative Organizations","304356.1 million baht · The budget will be used to support the Determining Plans and Process of Decentralization to Local Government Organization Act and its amendments, which authorize more decentralization of power and require efficient public services from local administrative organizations. Important actions include providing basic education, food supplement and lunch to school-aged children, supporting allowances for the elderly and persons with disabilities, and strengthening communities and the country.",""]],"40":[[1,"","4.3","Strategic Program on Promoting Integrated Development of Provinces and Clusters of Provinces","21727.7 million baht · The budget will be used to promote the integrated development of provinces and clusters of provinces in accordance with national development. Emphasis will be made on public participation to meet needs and solve area-based problems through projects under provincial and cluster development plans involving government, state enterprises, local administrative organizations, the private sector, and the people.",""]],"41":[[1,"","4.4","Integrated Program on Preparedness to Accommodate the Aging Society","448.7 million baht · The budget will be used to prepare the people for the aging society. Actions include publicizing health issues and preparation for aging, improving senior citizens' living quality through professional skills and income creation, strengthening social protection, improving family and community care, protecting the rights of the elderly, improving environments and infrastructure, and ensuring access to appropriate public health services.",""]],"42":[[1,"","4.5","Integrated Program on Development and Promotion of Local Economy","1474.3 million baht · The budget will be used to improve and strengthen the local economy to generate more earnings, diversify income to the locals, and narrow the income inequality gap by giving skill training and creating job opportunities. Support will be given to smart farmers, arable lands, entrepreneurs' capacity, agricultural learning centers, local products and services, and market mechanisms for community products.",""]],"43":[[1,"","4.6","Strategic Program on Creating Social Security","269465.2 million baht · The budget will be used to create social protection for the under-privileged and vulnerable groups as well as provide appropriate and fair social security and welfare. With a thorough health insurance system, people who hold the rights will be able to access medical and public health services, while social security and welfare for labor will also be improved and displaced people and beggars will receive help.",""]],"44":[[1,"","4.7","Strategic Program on Creating Equality in Education","81269.0 million baht · The budget will be used to increase access to quality and standard education. People will be ensured to receive basic education according to their rights, educational expenses from kindergarten until the highest level of basic education will be supported, satellite technology will be used to reduce education inequality, and support will be given to the Equitable Education Fund, learning centers, teachers and educators, and scholarships.",""]],"45":[[1,"","4.8","Strategic Program on Targeted Measures to Solve Group-Specific Problems","24026.1 million baht · The budget will be used to establish a system and mechanism to help people with special needs by supporting development of the system and investing in infrastructure applicable to each group. People with special needs will be ensured access to basic public services and equal social opportunity, while allowances and subsidies, low-income housing support, disability facilities and services, and renovation of rental buildings for low-income people will be provided.",""]],"46":[[1,"","4.9","Strategic Program on Supporting Creation of Social Opportunities and Equality","38942.8 million baht · The budget will be used to improve the quality of life of low-income people and farmers. People with the government welfare card will be able to access fundamentals for living, the National Saving Fund will encourage savings and pension benefits, members of cooperatives and farmer groups will receive interest reduction, and support will be given to trade cooperation, the Village and Urban Community Fund, and access to home loans for low-income households.",""]],"47":[[1,"","4.10","Fundamental Program on Creating Social Opportunities and Equality","1906.4 million baht · The budget will be used to support the Creation of Social Opportunity and Equity strategy in order to create equal opportunity to access public services, improve family institution, and create immunity for the people to have a good quality of lives. Supports will be given to community councils, workers' quality of life and social security, local wisdom, and fair trade.",""]],"48":[[1,"","4.11","Program on Public Sector Personnel","8295.3 million baht · The budget will be used to ensure efficiency and cost effectiveness in the management of public sector personnel. In addition, there will be development of the government agencies' work system and personnel capacity in order to perform their duties with efficiency, morality and ethics while maintaining their work-life balance.",""]],"49":[[1,"","5.1","Strategic Program on Creation of Sustainable Growth with Regard to Conservation, Rehabilitation and Prevention of Natural Resources Destruction","4732.0 million baht · The budget will be used to conserve and rehabilitate biodiversity. The strategy includes developing mechanisms and measures for conservation, prevention, protection, restoration, and sustainable use of biodiversity, promoting proper use of watershed areas, increasing green spaces and community forests, building networks of people to protect forests and forest fire, and helping people near forest areas including assigning land rights and providing arable land.",""]],"50":[[1,"","5.2","Strategic Program on Creation of Sustainable Growth of Marine Economic Society","189.7 million baht · The budget will be used to renovate, restore, and rebuild marine and coastal resources by increasing more eco-friendly marine activities, adding value to marine bio-based economy, restoring reefs and seagrass, protecting ecosystems and critically endangered marine life, and preserving marine and coastal ecosystem. Cooperation from the private sector and the people will be encouraged and marine tourism will be managed with regard to ecosystem capabilities.",""]],"51":[[1,"","5.3","Strategic Program on Coping with Repercussions from Climate Change","1574.8 million baht · The budget will be used to reduce Thailand greenhouse gases emission and reduce the impact of natural disasters and climate change. This will be done by promoting participation between various parties, improving the industrial sector's capacity in reducing pollution, increasing investment in low-carbon technology, and increasing carbon capture in forest areas.",""]],"52":[[1,"","5.4","Strategic Program on Dealing with Pollution and the Environment","567.6 million baht · The budget will be used to ensure that the country will have effective and quality environment management that is favorable for the good quality of life for the people. Waste and waste management problems will be systematically controlled, pollution will be regulated from its origin, air pollution will be administered to be within standards, and tools and mechanisms to prevent and reduce pollution will be developed.",""]],"53":[[1,"","5.5","Strategic Program on Elevating Paradigms to Stipulate the Future of the Country's Natural Resources and Environment","193.3 million baht · The budget will be used to enable Thai people to have desirable characteristics and behaviors regarding the environment and well-being. Emphasis will be on improving environmental assessment at the strategy level, promoting national and international stages to drive and discuss natural resources and environmental management, implementing policy and measure for land and soil resources management, and supporting decentralization and good governance in natural resources and environmental management and conservation.",""]],"54":[[1,"","5.6","Integrated Program on Management of Water Resources","54121.9 million baht · The budget will be used to increase the country's water security, ensure systematic and sustainable water resources management, balanced increase of water supply cost, and improve the productivity of water use. Focus will be made on addressing drought and saltwater intrusion, controlling water quality, increasing water supply through the Royal Rainmaking project, rehabilitating watershed forests, pushing forward relevant laws, and using water-related data to improve management efficiency.",""]],"55":[[1,"","5.7","Strategic Program on Supporting Creation of Growth on the Environmental-friendly Quality of Life","33033.7 million baht · The budget will be used for conserving, preserving, and properly and sustainably utilizing natural resources and the environment. Natural tourist attractions will be upgraded, water sources for the Royal Initiative Projects will be promoted, as well as irrigation management and land reformation for irrigation.",""]],"56":[[1,"","5.8","Fundamental Program on Creation of Growth on the Environmental-friendly Quality of Life","10111.9 million baht · The budget will be used for operations relating to natural resources and environment including preserving conservation areas and national reserved forest reserves to be evergreen, supporting land reformation and land and water resources management, supporting the Royal Rainmaking Project, establishing learning and plant conservation centers, and enhancing security of the mineral resource base.",""]],"57":[[1,"","5.9","Program on Public Sector Personnel","18440.0 million baht · The budget will be used to ensure efficiency and cost effectiveness in the management of public sector personnel. In addition, there will be development of the government agencies' work system and personnel capacity in order to perform their duties with efficiency, morality and ethics while maintaining their work-life balance.",""]],"58":[[1,"","6.1","Strategic Program on Improvement of Public Service Delivery and the Public Sector's Efficiency","28064.9 million baht · The budget will be used to improve public service delivery to be easy, convenient, quick, transparent, with low cost, and verifiable. Monetary and fiscal management, budgeting process, public debt management, monitoring and evaluation systems, public sector rebalancing, and public sector personnel development will be improved.",""]],"59":[[1,"","6.2","Integrated Program on Digital Government","2356.0 million baht · The budget will be used to improve government services through the use of digital technology with cost-effectiveness and people-centric in mind. Support will be given to development of government services that are valuable, functional, fast, convenient, efficient, transparent and verifiable, while government agencies and service systems will be connected and legal constraints will be reduced to become a digital government.",""]],"60":[[1,"","6.3","Integrated Program on Anti-corruption and Misconduct","498.0 million baht · The budget will be used to reduce the corruption problem in the Thai society through raising awareness and creating value for all sectors to be honest, ethical, and have good governance. Laws and regulations will be adjusted and enforced strictly and fairly, people will be able to participate in anti-corruption activities, and new technology will be used for monitoring corruption activities.",""]],"61":[[1,"","6.4","Strategic Program on Developing Laws and the Judicial Process","10225.5 million baht · The budget will be used to develop laws to be applicable in various contexts and changes, and enforce them transparently and effectively. Judicial process will be promoted and managed to be equal and fair by adopting innovation and digital technology, updating laws, improving participation in judicial process, protecting rights and liberty, and improving investigation and surveillance efficiency.",""]],"62":[[1,"","6.5","Strategic Program on Supporting Realignment for Balance and Development of Administrative System of the Public Sector","1579.8 million baht · The budget will be used to support the strategic goal on realignment for balance and development of the administrative system of the public sector by ensuring work culture of the public sector to focus on results and common interests and be responsive to the people needs. It will support downsizing the public sector, adopting big data technology and digital working processes, opening to public participation, encouraging integrity and thrift, and enforcing relevant and effective laws while managing the judicial process to be efficient and fair.",""]],"63":[[1,"","6.6","Fundamental Program on Realignment for Balance and Development of Administrative System of the Public Sector","432256.5 million baht · The budget will be used to carry out responsibilities on realigning and developing an administrative system to be efficient and cost effective, allowing public agencies to operate and provide standard services continuously with regards to its authority and laws while personnel, places of work, equipment and the working environment will be maintained in good condition.",""]],"64":[[1,"","6.7","Program on public Sector Personnel","183032.0 million baht · The budget will be used to ensure efficiency and cost effectiveness in the management of public sector personnel. In addition, there will be development of the government agencies' work system and personnel capacity in order to perform their duties with efficiency, morality and ethics while maintaining their work-life balance.",""]],"65":[[1,"","7.1","Program on Attending to Emergencies or Necessities","95900.0 million baht · The budget will be reserved as expenditures to prevent or rectify situations concerning people's peace and national security, as a public disaster relief fund, and for the state's urgent necessities with respect to fiscal discipline.",""]],"66":[[1,"","7.2","Program on Management of Public Debt","306618.0 million baht · The budget will be used to support the efficient management and repayment of public debt with maximum benefits to the economy.",""]]}});
PVD("thailand_budget_2024",{"docs":["","Table III-19 Expenditures by Budget Receiving Agency","Table I-4 Budget Allocation Strategy and Program FY 2024"],"s":{"1":[[1,"","1.1","Expenditures in relation to Royal Journeys and Visits, including Reception of Heads of States","800.0 million baht ",""]],"2":[[2,"","1.1","Strategic Program on Strengthening the Nation's Principal Institutions","12695.1 million baht · The budget will be used to instill everyone in the nation a conscience to cherish and treasure, maintain loyalty and uphold the nation's principal institutions. This includes protecting and upholding the monarchy, supporting royal initiatives and the Sufficiency Economy Philosophy, and supporting royal special activities.",""]],"3":[[2,"","1.2","Strategic Program on Maintaining Internal Peace","21144.3 million baht · The budget will be used to create security and safety in citizens' lives and properties by maintaining internal peace and domestic security. It emphasizes unity, support for territorial defense volunteers and local militias, crime prevention and suppression, law enforcement, justice, and public participation.",""]],"4":[[2,"","1.3","Strategic Program on Developing and Strengthening Politics in the Democratic Regime with the Monarchy as Head of State","396.0 million baht · The budget will be used to create political stability and good governance by promoting democracy and public participation. It also supports civic networks, election participation, and awareness of good citizenship under the democratic regime with the monarchy as head of state.",""]],"5":[[2,"","1.4","Integrated Program on Mobilization of Problem Rectification of Southern Border Provinces","6474.2 million baht · The budget will be used to create security and safety so people in the southern border provinces can live together peacefully in a multicultural society. It supports integrated problem-solving, justice and remedies, prevention of illegal activities, and development of agriculture, infrastructure, and vocational skills.",""]],"6":[[2,"","1.5","Strategic Program on Management of Problems of Alien Workforce and Human Trafficking","328.7 million baht · The budget will be used to prevent and solve human trafficking and forced labor problems and to systematically protect victims and risk groups. It also supports alien workforce management, labor inspection, victim assistance, and legal action against trafficking cases.",""]],"7":[[2,"","1.6","Integrated Program on Prevention, Suppression and Treatment of Drug Addiction","4254.5 million baht · The budget will be used to create immunity from narcotics for children, youth, workers, and risk groups and to prevent their involvement with drugs. It supports prevention, suppression, arrests, international cooperation, treatment, rehabilitation, and behavior development of offenders in drug-related offenses.",""]],"8":[[2,"","1.7","Strategic Program on Preventing and Rectifying Problems with Repercussions to the Security","19164.7 million baht · The budget will be used to address security problems so they no longer affect the administration and development of the country. It covers internal, border and coastal security, marine interests, cyber security, terrorism, transnational threats, nuclear and radiation threats, erosion prevention, and crime investigation.",""]],"9":[[2,"","1.8","Strategic Program on Developing National Preparedness System and Disaster Management System","21536.1 million baht · The budget will be used to improve emergency and rescue operations, minimize losses, and ensure safety in citizens' lives and properties. It supports disaster prevention and recovery capacity, warning systems, staff training, public awareness, disaster management, and riverbank erosion prevention.",""]],"10":[[2,"","1.9","Strategic Program on Developing National Defence Capacity and Preparedness in Coping with all Forms of Threats","54987.2 million baht · The budget will be used to prepare national security agencies to cope with all forms of threats. It supports intelligence and anti-intelligence capacity, intelligence technology, civil and private sector networks, armed forces capacity, and development of the national defense industry, military energy, research and development.",""]],"11":[[2,"","1.10","Strategic Program on Developing a Holistic Security Administration","423.3 million baht · The budget will be used to increase the efficiency of the security management mechanism. It promotes a holistic security mechanism to mobilize the National Security Policy and Plan.",""]],"12":[[2,"","1.11","Strategic Program on Promoting International Relations","5447.2 million baht · The budget will be used to enable Thailand to cope with external challenges and protect national interests through international-standard foreign affairs. It supports Thailand's role in ASEAN and the international community, economic and military cooperation, trade competitiveness, free trade areas, and science and innovation partnerships.",""]],"13":[[2,"","1.12","Fundamental Program on National Security","35226.2 million baht · The budget will be used to ensure efficient and cost-effective administration of national security missions and continuous service delivery according to legal authority and standards. It also supports personnel, workplaces, equipment, and the work environment.",""]],"14":[[2,"","1.13","Program on Public Sector Personnel","204072.1 million baht · The budget will be used to ensure efficiency and cost effectiveness in the management of public sector personnel. It also supports development of work systems and personnel capacity so duties are performed with efficiency, morality, and ethics while maintaining work-life balance.",""]],"15":[[1,"","1.2","Expenditures for Reimbursement of Emergency Financial Assistance to Disaster Victims","4000.0 million baht ",""]],"16":[[1,"","1.3","Expenditures under Royal Development Projects","2500.0 million baht ",""]],"17":[[1,"","1.4","Expenditures for Medical Care of Civil Servants, Employees and Public Personnel","79565.0 million baht ",""]],"18":[[1,"","1.5","Compensation for Construction Costs","800.0 million baht ",""]],"19":[[1,"","1.6","Financial Assistance for Civil Servants, Employees and Public Personnel","4520.0 million baht ",""]],"20":[[1,"","1.7","Pensions and Gratuities","333043.4 million baht ",""]],"21":[[1,"","1.8","Salary and Education Adjustments for Civil Servants","11000.0 million baht ",""]],"22":[[1,"","1.9","Contributions for Permanent Employees","440.0 million baht ",""]],"23":[[1,"","1.10","Financial Reserve, Contribution and Compensation for Civil Servants","78775.0 million baht ",""]],"24":[[1,"","1.11","Contingency Fund for Emergencies or Immediate Needs","99500.0 million baht ",""]],"25":[[1,"","1.12","Expenditures for Alleviating, Rectifying and Remedying those affected by the Outbreak of the Coronavirus 2019"," million baht ",""]],"26":[[2,"","2.1","Strategic Program on Value Creation Agriculture","49866.7 million baht · The budget will be used to expand agricultural GDP, increase productivity, and improve the capability to process products into high-value goods. It supports raising farmers' income, safe and environmentally friendly agriculture, technology adoption, agricultural research and development, and more stable farmer income.",""]],"27":[[2,"","2.2","Integrated Program on Development of Future Industries and Services","3800.3 million baht · The budget will be used to increase GDP growth and productivity in manufacturing and services throughout the supply chain. It supports bio-industry, digital economy and high technology industries, green industries, medical services, circular economy, EV production, power storage technology, and entrepreneur capacity development.",""]],"28":[[2,"","2.3","Integrated Program on Creating Income from Tourism","7310.3 million baht · The budget will be used to make tourism a mechanism for driving the country's economy. It supports sustainable tourism, creative and cultural tourism, regional connectivity, quality travelers, MICE, sports tourism, infrastructure improvement, and tourist safety.",""]],"29":[[2,"","2.4","Strategic Program on Area Development and Smart Livable City","9388.8 million baht · The budget will be used to improve Thailand's competitiveness by creating centers of economic and social prosperity in every region. It supports city development databases, environmental data platforms, smart city development, sustainable bio-industrial cities, and improved city facilities and safety.",""]],"30":[[2,"","2.5","Integrated Program on Development of Transport and Logistics System","122936.1 million baht · The budget will be used to provide efficient transportation and logistics systems and reduce logistics costs. It supports road, water, rail, and air infrastructure, public transportation, traffic solutions, logistics and supply chain management, trade facilitation, customs procedures, and logistics service capacity.",""]],"31":[[2,"","2.6","Strategic Program on Development of Transport and Logistics System","58055.7 million baht · The budget will be used to ensure efficient transportation and logistics systems by improving, refurbishing, and maintaining transport infrastructure. It supports highways, bridges, road safety, public transportation accessibility, and development of the Thailand Transport Data Center.",""]],"32":[[2,"","2.7","Strategic Program on Development of Energy Security","1856.2 million baht · The budget will be used to strengthen energy security and improve efficiency in national energy consumption. It supports renewable and alternative energy, energy infrastructure, clean energy production and consumption, efficient energy use, new energy sources, and related technology and regulatory improvements.",""]],"33":[[2,"","2.8","Strategic Program on Development of Digital Economy and Society","2428.5 million baht · The budget will be used to increase the value of digital businesses as a share of GDP. It supports digital infrastructure, broadband networks, international connectivity, big data centers, privacy and personal data protection, cyber threat measures, and digital skills for people in every occupation.",""]],"34":[[2,"","2.9","Strategic Program on Supporting Strong and Competitive Small and Medium-sized Enterprises","8710.7 million baht · The budget will be used to strengthen SMEs and community entrepreneurs with knowledge, skills, innovation, and digital capability. It supports access to finance, trade and investment abroad, matching funds for start-ups and SMEs, technology transfer, business model adjustment, and income generation in communities.",""]],"35":[[2,"","2.10","Strategic Program on Development of Special Economic Zones","446.3 million baht · The budget will be used to develop special economic zones as centers of economic and social prosperity. It supports infrastructure, customs checkpoint efficiency, legal and regulatory proposals, investor promotion, border public health, communicable disease control, labor skills, foreign worker systems, and digital technology adoption.",""]],"36":[[2,"","2.11","Integrated Program on Development of the Eastern Economic Corridor","7905.2 million baht · The budget will be used to support modern and environmentally friendly economic activities in the Eastern Economic Corridor. It supports efficient and connected infrastructure and public utilities, attractive and livable cities, better quality of life, and Thailand's role as a gateway to Asia.",""]],"37":[[2,"","2.12","Strategic Program on Innovation Research and Development","19066.4 million baht · The budget will be used to enable the public and private sectors to apply practical research and innovation results that respond to the country's needs. It supports standards and testing services, workforce development, conservation of resources, pollution and greenhouse gas management, and research management systems leading to benefits.",""]],"38":[[2,"","2.13","Strategic Program on Development of Science, Technology and Innovation Potentials","198.7 million baht · The budget will be used to move Thailand toward a knowledge-based economy by developing science and technology infrastructure and quality systems. It supports technology transfer, innovation, engineering design, and process and product development through cooperation among users, developers, and providers in the public and private sectors.",""]],"39":[[2,"","2.14","Strategic Program on Supporting the Development of Competitiveness","36964.5 million baht · The budget will be used to support the strategic goal of developing the country's competitiveness for stable and sustainable economic growth. It supports infrastructure, entrepreneur development, business model adaptation, new income and employment bases, trade and investment opportunities, and improved well-being.",""]],"40":[[2,"","2.15","Fundamental Program on the Development of Competitiveness","20435.2 million baht · The budget will be used to ensure efficient and cost-effective implementation of competitiveness development and continuous quality public services. It includes land and water management, trade promotion, standards and price control, entrepreneur development, tourism promotion, transport maintenance, and transport safety.",""]],"41":[[2,"","2.16","Program on Public Sector Personnel","42659.0 million baht · The budget will be used to ensure efficiency and cost effectiveness in the management of public sector personnel. It also supports development of work systems and personnel capacity so duties are performed with efficiency, morality, and ethics while maintaining work-life balance.",""]],"42":[[2,"","3.1","Strategic Program on Realignment of Value and Culture","3130.8 million baht · The budget will be used to enable Thai people to have good values, ethics, morality, public consciousness, and religious principles while adopting the Sufficiency Economy Philosophy in daily life. It also supports conservation of local culture and traditions and enhancement of Thailand's image internationally.",""]],"43":[[2,"","3.2","Strategic Program on Development of Human Potentials on a Life-Long Basis","33285.2 million baht · The budget will be used to improve Thai people's lives physically, mentally, and morally. It supports children and youth development, lifelong learning, and skill development for students and workers aligned with market standards and modern technology, while preparing the elderly to be self-reliant.",""]],"44":[[2,"","3.3","Strategic Program on Development of Education and Learning Quality","24770.5 million baht · The budget will be used to provide Thai people with a quality and standard education system. It supports reform of education and learning, teacher development, educational technology and platforms, STEM and language learning, vocational education, skill training, and quality sub-district schools.",""]],"45":[[2,"","3.4","Strategic Program on Good Public Health Promotion","64572.6 million baht · The budget will be used to provide people with good health and increase access to standard, universal, and efficient public health services. It supports training health personnel, modern medical technology, preparedness for emerging diseases, mental health care, emergency medical systems, village health volunteers, and Thai traditional medicine.",""]],"46":[[2,"","3.5","Strategic Program on Enhancing Sports Potentials","2420.4 million baht · The budget will be used to improve health and raise awareness of the benefits of exercise and basic sports. It supports exercise, sports, and recreation for all ages, development of sports personnel to international standards, youth excellence in sports, and sports infrastructure and equipment.",""]],"47":[[2,"","3.6","Strategic Program on Supporting Human Potentials Development and Reinforcement","561.9 million baht · The budget will be used to support Thai people to be quality citizens who can adapt to the modern era. It supports development of new and existing labor skills and promotes well-rounded development, good health, social responsibility, thirst for knowledge, and continuous self-improvement.",""]],"48":[[2,"","3.7","Fundamental Program on Human Potentials Development and Reinforcement","28433.7 million baht · The budget will be used to efficiently carry out missions and lawful powers in human resource development. It supports ethics and generosity, people potential development, improved quality and accessibility of education and learning systems, and promotion of good health.",""]],"49":[[2,"","3.8","Program on Public Sector Personnel","403992.0 million baht · The budget will be used to ensure efficiency and cost effectiveness in the management of public sector personnel. It also supports development of work systems and personnel capacity so duties are performed with efficiency, morality, and ethics while maintaining work-life balance.",""]],"50":[[2,"","4.1","Strategic Program on Social Empowerment","6823.0 million baht · The budget will be used to encourage every segment of society to participate more in social development. It supports community empowerment, strong families, social welfare organizations, volunteers and civil society, women's role and human rights, local management, housing and arable land, and conservation of local arts and cultures.",""]],"51":[[2,"","4.2","Strategic Program on Decentralization to the Local Administrative Organizations","337309.8 million baht · The budget will be used to support decentralization by increasing subsidies to local government organizations so they can provide efficient public services and become self-sustained. It includes support for local schools, milk and lunch for school-aged children, allowances for the elderly and persons with disabilities, and stronger community roles.",""]],"52":[[2,"","4.3","Strategic Program on Promoting Integrated Development of Provinces and Clusters of Provinces","23031.7 million baht · The budget will be used to promote integrated development of provinces and clusters of provinces in line with national development. It emphasizes public participation and area-based problem solving through provincial development plans covering economic, social, security, and environmental dimensions.",""]],"53":[[2,"","4.4","Integrated Program on Preparedness to Accommodate the Aging Society","820.1 million baht · The budget will be used to prepare people for an aging society. It supports health awareness, improved living quality and income opportunities for senior citizens, social systems and rights protection, family and community care, age-friendly environments and infrastructure, and access to appropriate healthcare services and innovations.",""]],"54":[[2,"","4.5","Strategic Program on Development and Promotion of Local Economy","2296.0 million baht · The budget will be used to strengthen the local economy, generate more earnings, distribute income locally, and reduce inequality. It supports skill training, job opportunities, smart farmers, arable land, entrepreneur capacity, product development, local processing, and improved markets and management mechanisms for community products.",""]],"55":[[2,"","4.6","Strategic Program on Creating Social Security","343057.8 million baht · The budget will be used to provide basic medical services near people's homes and ensure good health through the upgraded 30-baht universal healthcare scheme. It also supports fair access to health services, consumer protection, social security and welfare for formal and informal workers, work safety, and assistance for displaced people and beggars.",""]],"56":[[2,"","4.7","Strategic Program on Creating Equality in Education","85848.5 million baht · The budget will be used to increase access to quality and standard education and support educational expenses from kindergarten to the highest level of basic education. It also supports the Equitable Education Fund, learning centers, local cooperation mechanisms, teacher development, and scholarships for higher education.",""]],"57":[[2,"","4.8","Strategic Program on Targeted Measures to Solve Group-Specific Problems","22863.1 million baht · The budget will be used to develop systems and infrastructure suited to each group of people and to ensure vulnerable groups have access to fair basic public services. It supports rights verification, allowances and subsidies, housing support, disability services, help for people facing social problems, and improved access to public services.",""]],"58":[[2,"","4.9","Strategic Program on Supporting Creation of Social Opportunities and Equality","5038.0 million baht · The budget will be used to improve the quality of life of low-income people and farmers. It supports access to basic necessities for welfare card holders, agricultural land for small farmers, interest reduction for cooperative members and farmer groups, community economy development, village and urban community funds, home loans for low-income households, and funeral ceremonies bestowed by royal grace.",""]],"59":[[2,"","4.10","Fundamental Program on Creating Social Opportunities and Equality","837.9 million baht · The budget will be used to support the strategy by creating equal opportunity to access public services. It supports participation through community councils, improved quality of life and social security for workers, land bank creation, and knowledge transfer to improve farmers' and people's capability according to the Sufficiency Economy Philosophy.",""]],"60":[[2,"","4.11","Program on Public Sector Personnel","8456.6 million baht · The budget will be used to ensure efficiency and cost effectiveness in the management of public sector personnel. It also supports development of work systems and personnel capacity so duties are performed with efficiency, morality, and ethics while maintaining work-life balance.",""]],"61":[[2,"","5.1","Strategic Program on Creation of Sustainable Growth with Regard to Conservation, Rehabilitation and Prevention of Natural Resources Destruction","5640.6 million baht · The budget will be used to conserve and rehabilitate biodiversity. It supports conservation, protection, restoration, and sustainable use of biodiversity, forest conservation and expansion of green areas, mangrove protection, promotion of economic woods, and land and forest management planning.",""]],"62":[[2,"","5.2","Strategic Program on Creation of Sustainable Growth of Marine Economic Society","414.4 million baht · The budget will be used to renovate, restore, and rebuild marine and coastal resources. It supports seawater quality management, protection of ecosystems and endangered marine life, preservation of marine and coastal ecosystems, and systems for tracking and assessing oil spill impacts.",""]],"63":[[2,"","5.3","Strategic Program on Coping with Repercussions from Climate Change","1767.6 million baht · The budget will be used to reduce greenhouse gas emissions and lessen the impact of natural disasters and climate change. It supports climate-friendly growth, participation across sectors, industrial pollution reduction, low-carbon investment, increased carbon capture in forests, and improved weather monitoring and alert systems.",""]],"64":[[2,"","5.4","Strategic Program on Dealing with Pollution and the Environment","836.2 million baht · The budget will be used to ensure effective and quality environmental management favorable to people's quality of life. It supports waste management, pollution prevention and control at the source, reduction of agricultural burning, air quality monitoring, wastewater treatment, and environmental health in hospitals.",""]],"65":[[2,"","5.5","Strategic Program on Elevating Paradigms to Stipulate the Future of the Country's Natural Resources and Environment","63.3 million baht · The budget will be used to manage land resources, promote environmentally friendly production and consumption, create discipline and participation in waste management, raise awareness of climate change, and improve the efficiency of environmental impact assessments.",""]],"66":[[2,"","5.6","Integrated Program on Management of Water Resources","56087.4 million baht · The budget will be used to increase water security, ensure systematic and sustainable water resources management, and address drought. It supports alternative water sources, water distribution, flood management, wastewater management, watershed conservation and restoration, soil erosion prevention, and afforestation.",""]],"67":[[2,"","5.7","Strategic Program on Management of Water Resources","35728.2 million baht · The budget will be used for development, restoration, improvement, and repair of irrigation and water distribution systems. It also supports water management and irrigation works, management of water sources in and out of irrigation areas and in communities, aircraft for the Royal Rainmaking project, and information technology for water management.",""]],"68":[[2,"","5.8","Strategic Program on Supporting Creation of Growth on the Environmental-friendly Quality of Life","2318.9 million baht · The budget will be used for conserving, preserving, and properly and sustainably utilizing natural resources and the environment. It also supports water management, information technology for water management, and improved groundwater resources management.",""]],"69":[[2,"","5.9","Fundamental Program on Creation of Growth on the Environmental-friendly Quality of Life","9949.6 million baht · The budget will be used for operations relating to environmentally friendly quality of life growth. It supports management of water resources, natural resources, pollution, and the environment, greenhouse gas management, and learning and plant conservation centers.",""]],"70":[[2,"","5.10","Program on Public Sector Personnel","18214.3 million baht · The budget will be used to ensure efficiency and cost effectiveness in the management of public sector personnel. It also supports development of work systems and personnel capacity so duties are performed with efficiency, morality, and ethics while maintaining work-life balance.",""]],"71":[[2,"","6.1","Strategic Program on Improvement of Public Service Delivery and the Public Sector's Efficiency","28383.5 million baht · The budget will be used to improve public service delivery so it is easy, convenient, quick, transparent, low-cost, and verifiable. It supports monetary and fiscal management, tax system improvement, budgeting and public debt management, monitoring and evaluation, public sector rebalancing, and personnel development under the moral system.",""]],"72":[[2,"","6.2","Integrated Program on Digital Government","2806.1 million baht · The budget will be used to improve government services through digital technology with cost-effectiveness and people-centric service in mind. It supports connected government services, approval and authorization systems, data storage and open data, and legal adjustments to enable digital government.",""]],"73":[[2,"","6.3","Integrated Program on Anti-corruption and Misconduct","712.4 million baht · The budget will be used to reduce corruption in Thai society by raising awareness and creating values of honesty, ethics, and good governance. It supports legal enforcement, public participation in prevention and surveillance, anti-corruption networks, and use of new technology to monitor corruption.",""]],"74":[[2,"","6.4","Strategic Program on Developing Laws and the Judicial Process","17709.7 million baht · The budget will be used to develop laws so they are applicable to changing contexts and enforced transparently and effectively. It supports equal and fair judicial processes, innovation and digital technology in justice, removal of unnecessary laws, rights protection, and more transparent investigation and surveillance.",""]],"75":[[2,"","6.5","Strategic Program on Supporting Realignment for Balance and Development of Administrative System of the Public Sector","428826.0 million baht · The budget will be used to support the strategic goal of a public sector focused on results and common interests and responsive to people's needs with ease, speed, and transparency. It supports downsizing, anti-corruption, big data and digital processes, public participation, integrity, updated laws, and efficient and fair judicial management.",""]],"76":[[2,"","6.6","Fundamental Program on Realignment for Balance and Development of Administrative System of the Public Sector","21371.0 million baht · The budget will be used to carry out responsibilities on realigning and developing the administrative system efficiently and cost effectively. It supports continuous standard services in line with authority and laws while maintaining personnel, workplaces, equipment, and the working environment.",""]],"77":[[2,"","6.7","Program on public Sector Personnel","108401.8 million baht · The budget will be used to ensure efficiency and cost effectiveness in the management of public sector personnel. It also supports development of work systems and personnel capacity so duties are performed with efficiency, morality, and ethics while maintaining work-life balance.",""]],"78":[[2,"","7.1","Program on Attending to Emergencies or Necessities","100300.0 million baht · The budget will be reserved to prevent or rectify situations concerning people's peace and national security, provide public disaster relief, meet urgent state necessities, and compensate construction costs to assist construction business operators in line with fiscal discipline.",""]],"79":[[2,"","7.2","Program on Management of Public Debt","346380.1 million baht · The budget will be used to support efficient management and repayment of public debt with maximum benefits to the economy.",""]],"80":[[2,"","7.3","Program on Expenditures for Replenishment of Treasury Account Balance","118361.1 million baht · The budget will be used to reimburse expenditures withdrawn from the treasury account in accordance with the Treasury Account Act of B.E. 2491 (A.D. 1948) and its amendments.",""]]}});
PVD("thailand_budget_2025",{"docs":["","Table I-4 Budget Allocation Strategy and Program FY 2025"],"s":{"1":[[1,"","1.1","Strategic Program on Strengthening the Nation's Principal Institutions","12695.6 million baht · The amount will be allocated to foster loyalty, honesty, and commitment among Thai people to uphold the nation's principal institutions, and provide security to the King and royal family. This includes instilling awareness and appreciation of the significance of the nation's principal institutions, incorporating knowledge based on royal initiatives and the Sufficiency Economy Philosophy to develop and address regional problems, and supporting royal special activities.",""]],"2":[[1,"","1.2","Strategic Program on Maintaining Internal Peace","28355.0 million baht · The amount will be allocated to ensure security and safety for the public by enhancing the safety of lives and property and human security. The program focuses on supporting the mission of the Territorial Defense Volunteers and Local Militias, driving government policies using village mechanisms, increasing the efficiency of crime prevention and suppression operations and law enforcement, encouraging public participation from all sectors, and providing justice and services.",""]],"3":[[1,"","1.3","Strategic Program on Developing and Strengthening Politics in the Democratic Regime with the Monarchy as Head of State","721.7 million baht · The amount will be allocated to enhance political stability and good governance by promoting the development and strengthening democratic politics. Focus will be on public relations for democracy development, public participation and network strengthening in the election process, and instilling in citizens the knowledge and understanding necessary to participate and fulfill their roles as good citizens within the democratic regime with the monarchy as head of state.",""]],"4":[[1,"","1.4","Integrated Program on Mobilization of Problem Rectification of Southern Border Provinces","5737.9 million baht · The amount will be allocated to bring peace to the southern region, ensure national security, and guarantee the safety of life and property for the people in the area, creating peaceful coexistence within a multicultural society. The strategy involves a systematic and integrated approach to solving problems and promoting development in the southern border provinces, including safety, intelligence operations, justice, fair assistance, prohibition of illegal acts, area development, career skills, and support for joint activities under a strong multicultural society.",""]],"5":[[1,"","1.5","Strategic Program on Management of Problems of Alien Workforce and Human Trafficking","402.7 million baht · The amount will be allocated to resolve the security problems associated with human trafficking. It seeks to provide systematic protection and assistance to victims of trafficking, child labor, forced labor, and vulnerable groups, and to prevent and combat human trafficking using rights, freedom, and human rights mechanisms.",""]],"6":[[1,"","1.6","Integrated Program on Prevention, Suppression and Treatment of Drug Addiction","5099.0 million baht · The amount will be allocated to address drug issues so they no longer impact national administration and development. It includes creating a protective environment for children, youth, workers, and at-risk populations, organizing mechanisms to prevent and solve problems systematically, suppressing producers and traffickers, strengthening international cooperation, and providing treatment, rehabilitation, reconditioning, and follow-up assistance for drug addicts.",""]],"7":[[1,"","1.7","Strategic Program on Preventing and Rectifying Problems with Repercussions to the Security","18215.3 million baht · The amount will be allocated to address security-related issues so they do not affect the country's administration and development. This includes maintaining internal security, protecting interests relating to natural resources and the environment on land and at sea, ensuring cybersecurity, securing border areas, combating transnational crime and terrorism, providing maritime security, enhancing nuclear and radiation safety, and improving surveillance, response, and crime suppression.",""]],"8":[[1,"","1.8","Strategic Program on Developing National Preparedness System and Disaster Management System","24537.7 million baht · The amount will be allocated to build public confidence in emergency and rescue operations, minimize loss, and ensure safety in citizens' lives and properties. Efforts will focus on developing and improving policies and management to cover all types of disasters, preparing for disaster relief and emergency response, training personnel, developing an inclusive warning system, improving communication, increasing efficiency in solving disaster problems, and constructing dams to protect river banks.",""]],"9":[[1,"","1.9","Strategic Program on Developing National Defense Capacity and Preparedness in Coping with all Forms of Threats","60339.5 million baht · The amount will be allocated to ensure that security agencies are better prepared to face all types of threats in all dimensions. It aims to increase the efficiency of intelligence agencies and the intelligence community through strengthening and developing the national defense system, enhancing cooperation and resource pooling from all sectors, emphasizing the armed forces' capacity in national development and public assistance, and promoting the military defense and energy industry along with research and development for defense technology.",""]],"10":[[1,"","1.10","Strategic Program on Developing a Holistic Security Administration Mechanism","406.0 million baht · The amount will be allocated to enhance the efficiency of security management mechanisms. The National Security Policy and Plan will be driven by developing a holistic security management mechanism.",""]],"11":[[1,"","1.11","Strategic Program on Promoting International Relations","5581.4 million baht · The amount will be allocated to unify Thailand's foreign affairs to achieve national security, prosperity, sustainability, international standards, and prestige in the global community. Focus will be on safeguarding national interests, promoting Thailand's role in Asia and ASEAN, supporting sustainable development, military relations, trade competitiveness, free-trade areas, and cooperation in science, technology, and innovation.",""]],"12":[[1,"","1.12","Fundamental Program on National Security","38963.8 million baht · The amount will be allocated to ensure efficient and cost-effective administration of national security missions and enable government agencies to continuously perform and provide services according to their legal mandate and standards. It also supports taking good care of personnel, workplaces, equipment, and the work environment.",""]],"13":[[1,"","1.13","Program on Public Sector Personnel","202812.4 million baht · The amount will be allocated to ensure efficiency and cost effectiveness in the management of public sector personnel. In addition, there will be development of the government agencies' work system and personnel competencies so they can perform their duties with efficiency, morality and ethics while maintaining work-life balance.",""]],"14":[[1,"","2.1","Strategic Program on Value Creation Agriculture","14396.1 million baht · The amount will be allocated to increase the growth of the agricultural sector's GDP and enhance agricultural productivity and transform it into high-value downstream products by using technology to strengthen and sustain agricultural resources. The program promotes research, development, safety standards, organic farming, conservation of agricultural biological resources, value addition, integrated production management, new-generation farmers, and stronger farmer groups to generate income and improve quality of life.",""]],"15":[[1,"","2.2","Integrated Program on Development of Future Industries and Services","8698.5 million baht · The amount will be allocated to increase the growth rate of GDP in the industrial and service sectors and enhance productivity in these sectors. It promotes bio-industry, entrepreneurs and high-tech labor, comprehensive medical services, research and innovation in digital, data and artificial intelligence, transportation industry transition, technology transfer, joint ventures, industrial zones, workforce development, skilled labor import, advanced technology investment, and security industries with economic potential.",""]],"16":[[1,"","2.3","Strategic Program on Promoting and Developing Tourism Potential","3134.8 million baht · The amount will be allocated to elevate Thailand's tourism competitiveness, increase the tourism sector's contribution to GDP, and boost tourism revenue in secondary cities. This involves developing the tourism ecosystem, enhancing safety standards, restoring natural tourist attractions, developing infrastructure, preparing communities and personnel, promoting Thailand's tourism image and soft power, and positioning Thailand as a destination for conferences, trade shows, and international events.",""]],"17":[[1,"","2.4","Integrated Program on Creating Income from Tourism","8132.8 million baht · The amount will be allocated to increase the contribution of the tourism sector to GDP, enhance tourism revenue in secondary cities, and improve Thailand's tourism competitiveness. It focuses on spreading tourism activities and income to local communities, developing sustainable, health, creative and cultural tourism, preserving Thai identity, supporting international standards in tourist destinations and establishments, valuing the environment, ensuring tourist safety, and combating corruption and unfair practices in the tourism sector.",""]],"18":[[1,"","2.5","Strategic Program on Area Development and Smart Livable City","13003.7 million baht · The amount will be allocated to enhance Thailand's competitiveness and create centers of economic and social prosperity in every region of the country. This will be achieved by developing transportation, communication, and energy systems using modern digital technology, distributing prosperity, ensuring ecological zoning plans, stabilizing rural living conditions, promoting sustainable agriculture and eco-industries, conserving natural resources and cultural identity, and creating urban development databases.",""]],"19":[[1,"","2.6","Integrated Program on Development of Transport and Logistics System","103120.5 million baht · The amount will be allocated to provide Thailand with an efficient transportation and logistics system to reduce logistics costs and enhance competitiveness. It includes developing transportation infrastructure across road, water, rail, and air, multimodal facilities, public transport systems, logistics and supply chain management, trade facilitation, customs procedures, electronic data linkage, and the capabilities of logistics service providers and international transport networks.",""]],"20":[[1,"","2.7","Strategic Program on Improvement of Transportation Efficiency","92799.6 million baht · The amount will be allocated to provide Thailand with modern and efficient transportation systems and facilities. This will be achieved through the development, improvement, and maintenance of transportation infrastructure across road, water, rail, and air, development of facilities to support multimodal transportation, improved access to public transportation, and the production and oversight of transportation personnel.",""]],"21":[[1,"","2.8","Strategic Program on Development of Energy Security","1957.9 million baht · The amount will be allocated to enable Thailand to have energy security and improve efficiency in the country's energy consumption. This will be achieved by promoting and developing factors for energy procurement and infrastructure, supporting technology for energy management, promoting renewable and alternative energy, improving energy efficiency across all sectors, encouraging behavior change, supporting fair competition in the energy market, restructuring energy prices, and improving laws and regulations related to new energy technologies and business models.",""]],"22":[[1,"","2.9","Strategic Program on Development of Digital Economy and Society","2526.3 million baht · The strategic plan aims to increase the value of digital businesses in relation to GDP and expand the domestic digital economy. It will do so by developing nationwide digital infrastructure, promoting investment and shared use of digital infrastructure resources, developing international-standard digital infrastructure and data centers, updating laws, protecting personal rights and data, implementing cyber threat measures, and promoting education and skill enhancement in technology.",""]],"23":[[1,"","2.10","Strategic Program on Supporting Strong and Competitive Small and Medium-sized Enterprises","4758.7 million baht · The amount will be allocated to transform entrepreneurs at all levels into modern entrepreneurs who play a significant role in the economy. The program seeks to strengthen SME and community entrepreneurs through innovation, digital technology, market access, capital funding, financial products, export promotion, distribution centers, market knowledge, investment in research and innovation, technology transfer, public-private collaboration, job creation, and income opportunities for communities nationwide.",""]],"24":[[1,"","2.11","Strategic Program on Development of Special Economic Zones","428.4 million baht · The amount will be allocated to develop the special economic zones as centers of economic and social prosperity by providing infrastructure in transportation, social, environment and education, and increasing the efficiency of customs checkpoints and updating or proposing laws and regulations. Attention will also be given to publicizing targeted areas to investors, improving public health at border areas, preventing communicable diseases, developing labor skills, organizing foreign workers systems, and preparing border areas for connected economic and social activities through digital technology and innovation.",""]],"25":[[1,"","2.12","Integrated Program on Development of the Eastern Economic Corridor","7329.9 million baht · The amount will be allocated to promote the growth of the gross regional product and increase investment in the Eastern Economic Corridor. The program encourages the development of modern, environmentally friendly economic activities, efficient and connected infrastructure and public utilities, livable and modern cities, improved quality of life for residents, and a stronger role for Thailand as a gateway to Asia in the global context.",""]],"26":[[1,"","2.13","Strategic Program on Innovation Research and Development","19254.5 million baht · The amount will be allocated to enhance the country's competitiveness in technology and scientific infrastructure and increase the value of research and innovation investment in relation to GDP. The actions include emphasizing research and innovation that meet national needs, promoting the private sector's role and collaboration with educational institutions, developing internationally recognized standards and testing services, addressing the digital era and aging society, developing highly skilled labor, conserving biodiversity, managing pollution and greenhouse gases, and improving research management systems for practical application.",""]],"27":[[1,"","2.14","Strategic Program on Development of Science, Technology and Innovation Potentials","254.9 million baht · The amount will be allocated to increase the number of modern science and technology infrastructures necessary for the country's development. The program focuses on developing modern infrastructure and facilities, internationally recognized quality and testing systems, technology and innovation transfer, engineering design, process and product development through consortium operations, production and development of science and technology personnel, and collaboration among researchers, educational institutions, research institutes, and government agencies.",""]],"28":[[1,"","2.15","Strategic Program on Supporting the Development of Competitiveness","23714.0 million baht · The amount will be allocated to support the strategic goal of developing the country's competitiveness so Thailand becomes a developed country with stable and sustainable economic growth. This will be achieved by elevating the country's potential in the economy, identity, culture, tradition, way of life, natural resources, and comparative advantages, integrating technology and innovation, developing infrastructure in transportation, logistics, science, technology, digital systems and environmental adjustments, enhancing entrepreneurs, creating new income and employment bases, expanding trade and investment opportunities, and improving people's well-being.",""]],"29":[[1,"","2.16","Fundamental Program on the Development of Competitiveness","15346.2 million baht · The amount will be allocated to ensure the efficiency and cost-effectiveness of the country's competitiveness enhancement missions and allow government agencies to operate and provide services continuously in line with their legal authority and standards. It also ensures that personnel, facilities, equipment, and working environments are well-maintained.",""]],"30":[[1,"","2.17","Program on Public Sector Personnel","43343.1 million baht · The amount will be allocated to ensure efficiency and cost effectiveness in the management of public sector personnel. In addition, there will be development of the government agencies' work system and personnel capacity so they can perform their duties with efficiency, morality and ethics while maintaining work-life balance.",""]],"31":[[1,"","3.1","Strategic Program on Realignment of Value and Culture","2938.6 million baht · The amount will be allocated to instill in citizens good morals, ethics, values, and culture, fostering a public spirit and social responsibility. It encourages the integration of religious principles and the philosophy of sufficiency economy into daily life, the conservation and restoration of customs and traditions, and support for cultural heritage development to increase value and enhance Thailand's image internationally.",""]],"32":[[1,"","3.2","Strategic Program on Development of Human Potentials on a Life-Long Basis","36017.8 million baht · The amount will be allocated to ensure that individuals of all ages can develop to their full potential, and that families and communities are strong and secure. The program promotes well-being and age-appropriate development from pregnancy through early childhood, quality education and lifelong learning, workforce skills aligned with the labor market and modern technology, and occupational skills for the elderly so they can be self-reliant.",""]],"33":[[1,"","3.3","Strategic Program on Development of Education and Learning Quality","34122.8 million baht · The amount will be allocated to provide Thai people with quality education that meets standards. This will be achieved by developing curricula, learning models, and teaching methods for the 21st century, supporting digital technology and innovation, promoting students' potential based on aptitude and multiple intelligences, developing teachers and educational personnel, preparing highly skilled professionals for the labor market, and supporting quality schools to expand access and reduce educational inequality.",""]],"34":[[1,"","3.4","Strategic Program on Good Public Health Promotion","66518.9 million baht · The amount will be allocated to ensure that Thai people have good physical and mental health, with access to standard, comprehensive, and efficient public health services. The program promotes training and distribution of medical personnel, development of modern healthcare services and tools, mental health care systems, emergency medical and referral systems, village health volunteer capacity, and traditional Thai medicine, alternative medicine, and Thai herbs for medical benefits.",""]],"35":[[1,"","3.5","Strategic Program on Enhancing Sports Potentials","2739.0 million baht · The amount will be allocated to ensure that Thai people have good health and to raise awareness of the benefits of exercise and basic sports. Emphasis will be made on promoting exercise, sports, and recreational activities among citizens of all ages, supporting sports and sport science personnel to align with international standards, empowering youth to excel as professional athletes, and supporting sports and recreation infrastructure, equipment, and venues.",""]],"36":[[1,"","3.6","Strategic Program on Supporting Human Potentials Development and Reinforcement","455.2 million baht · The amount will be allocated to support the strategic goal of developing and reinforcing human resource potential. It focuses on developing Thai people of all ages to be good, capable, and high-quality individuals who can access a comprehensive and quality education system, elevating education management, and developing large databases and information technology networks in education.",""]],"37":[[1,"","3.7","Fundamental Program on Human Potentials Development and Reinforcement","23473.4 million baht · The amount will be provided to efficiently and cost-effectively carry out missions and lawful power in human resource development. The program promotes quality of life and education for all age groups, supports teachers and educational personnel, establishes systems for monitoring, preventing, and controlling diseases and health hazards, develops health management systems, promotes sports potential, conserves cultural heritage, and supports Buddhism and religious objects.",""]],"38":[[1,"","3.8","Program on Public Sector Personnel","416438.4 million baht · The amount will be allocated to ensure efficiency and cost effectiveness in the management of public sector personnel. In addition, there will be development of the government agencies' work system and personnel capacity so they can perform their duties with efficiency, morality and ethics while maintaining work-life balance.",""]],"39":[[1,"","4.1","Strategic Program on Social Empowerment","7199.3 million baht · The amount will be allocated to promote community empowerment as a social force and increase participation from all sectors in social development. The program supports strong families, ending domestic violence, youth contribution, network development, management mechanisms at local levels, promotion of women and human rights, social enterprises, Sufficiency Economy Philosophy-based community development, job and income security, royal initiative projects, and operational networks to promote social capital and local wisdom.",""]],"40":[[1,"","4.2","Strategic Program on Decentralization to the Local Administrative Organizations","370265.5 million baht · The amount will be allocated to align with the decentralization law and promote the decentralization of authority to local governments so they can be self-sufficient in all dimensions. The target is to ensure that citizens receive comprehensive public services from local governments through support for education, milk and lunches, living allowances for the elderly and disabled, wastewater and garbage management, and promotion of agriculture, tourism, industry, trade, investment, and policy linkage between regional and central parts.",""]],"41":[[1,"","4.3","Strategic Program on Promoting Integrated Development of Provinces and Clusters of Provinces","24024.2 million baht · The amount will be allocated to develop provinces into centers of economic, social, and technological growth. Focus will be on empowering citizens to determine the direction of area development and integrating plans from villages to regional groups so development meets local needs and solves area-specific problems, elevates quality of life, distributes income evenly, and creates economic value from local resource potential sustainably.",""]],"42":[[1,"","4.4","Integrated Program on Preparedness to Accommodate the Aging Society","870.1 million baht · The amount will be allocated to prepare the pre-elderly population to enter old age with quality and security. This is achieved by promoting knowledge in economics, society, and health, developing supportive environments, enhancing long-term care services, encouraging participation from all sectors, supporting local governments and caregivers, enhancing job skills and employment opportunities for the elderly, strengthening health care systems using technology and innovation, and creating model care systems and central databases.",""]],"43":[[1,"","4.5","Strategic Program on Development and Promotion of Local Economy","2085.8 million baht · The amount will be allocated to continuously and appropriately distribute and increase the income of farmers, households, communities, and low-income individuals. This will be achieved by promoting knowledge and skills, developing smart farmers and entrepreneurial skills, supporting private sector knowledge transfer, increasing income and reducing expenses through digital technology, improving land allocation efficiency, promoting valuable trees and bioproducts, developing community products and agro-processing, and creating marketing channels through cooperatives, community stores, and community enterprises.",""]],"44":[[1,"","4.6","Strategic Program on Land and Soil Resource Management","1695.4 million baht · The amount will be allocated to develop mechanisms for the utilization of public land for the management of the country's land and soil resources. This includes developing land trustee mechanisms, land reform areas, public spaces and degraded forest areas, increasing equitable access to agricultural land ownership, developing approaches for land rights verification and land title documents, amending relevant laws, and generating balanced and sustainable income from land through participatory processes.",""]],"45":[[1,"","4.7","Strategic Program on Creating Social Security","378128.7 million baht · The amount will be allocated to provide citizens with convenient access to basic medical services close to home. It enhances the 30-baht universal healthcare scheme, ensures access to comprehensive and standard medical and public health services using only an ID card, improves consumer protection, promotes social security and welfare for formal and informal workers, creates appropriate workplace safety and health conditions, supports public welfare spending for low-income individuals, and promotes equal access to justice and legal assistance.",""]],"46":[[1,"","4.8","Strategic Program on Creating Equality in Education","88530.8 million baht · The amount will be allocated to create opportunities for equitable access to quality and standard education. It ensures access to basic education within and outside the formal system, supports educational expenses from kindergarten through completion of basic education, promotes education for children and youth outside the school system, supports the Equitable Education Fund for the underprivileged and disadvantaged, improves education quality in formal and informal systems, develops teachers and educational personnel, and supports scholarships for higher education opportunities.",""]],"47":[[1,"","4.9","Strategic Program on Targeted Measures to Solve Group-Specific Problems","29685.7 million baht · The amount will be allocated to establish systems and mechanisms to care for target groups requiring special assistance, such as children, youth, women, the elderly, people with disabilities, and the underprivileged. It supports social protection systems and welfare services, financial aid, centers to expedite public welfare services, collaboration and public participation, allowances and subsidies, housing support for low-income groups, facilities and public services for people with disabilities, assistance for those facing social problems, and safer public transportation.",""]],"48":[[1,"","4.10","Strategic Program on Supporting Creation of Social Opportunities and Equality","14454.0 million baht · The amount will be allocated to sustainably improve the quality of life for low-income individuals and farmers. This is achieved by supporting the allocation of agricultural land for ownership, farming and housing, addressing land rights loss, promoting innovative land management models, supporting loans for agricultural occupations, promoting the Village and Urban Community Fund, and organizing funeral ceremonies bestowed by royal grace.",""]],"49":[[1,"","4.11","Fundamental Program on Creating Social Opportunities and Equality","716.9 million baht · The amount will be allocated to support the Creation of Social Opportunity and Equity strategy. The program supports high-performance management systems, digital-era skills for government personnel, equal and comprehensive access to public services, establishment of a land bank, knowledge for farmers and citizens according to the Sufficiency Economy Philosophy, protection of workers' rights, and proper safety and occupational health management in workplaces.",""]],"50":[[1,"","4.12","Program on Public Sector Personnel","8610.4 million baht · The amount will be allocated to ensure efficiency and cost effectiveness in the management of public sector personnel. In addition, there will be development of the government agencies' work systems and personnel capacity so they can perform their duties with efficiency, morality, and ethics while maintaining work-life balance.",""]],"51":[[1,"","5.1","Strategic Program on Creation of Sustainable Growth with Regard to Conservation, Rehabilitation and Prevention of Natural Resources Destruction","5677.8 million baht · The amount will be allocated to conserve and restore biodiversity. The strategy includes developing mechanisms and measures for conservation, prevention, protection, risk mitigation, restoration, and sustainable utilization of biodiversity; preserving forest areas; promoting sustainable consumption and production; increasing green spaces; promoting economic tree planting; enhancing mangrove conservation and restoration; and drafting land and forest management plans to mitigate conflicts over resource utilization.",""]],"52":[[1,"","5.2","Strategic Program on Creation of Sustainable Growth of Marine Economic Society","603.2 million baht · The amount will be given to improve, restore, and rebuild marine and coastal resources. This involves managing seawater quality, reducing waste and pollutants entering the sea, protecting ecosystems and critically endangered marine life, restoring marine and coastal ecosystems, and developing systems for tracking, monitoring, predicting, and assessing the impact of oil spills in the sea.",""]],"53":[[1,"","5.3","Strategic Program on Coping with Repercussions from Climate Change","2077.3 million baht · The amount will be allocated to enable the country to reduce greenhouse gas emissions and mitigate the effects of natural disasters. The strategy focuses on enhancing adaptation capacity, promoting sustainable growth in a climate-friendly society, stakeholder participation, reducing pollution and greenhouse gas emissions from industry, promoting low-carbon technology and climate-friendly infrastructure investment, increasing carbon sequestration in forest areas, improving weather monitoring and early warning systems, and supporting adaptation measures to minimize losses and damages.",""]],"54":[[1,"","5.4","Strategic Program on Dealing with Pollution and the Environment","872.3 million baht · The amount will be allocated to ensure that the country has effective and quality environmental management favorable to a good quality of life. Waste management problems will be controlled more systematically and efficiently, pollution will be prevented and regulated at its sources, agricultural land will be managed to reduce burning, air pollution will be kept within standards, air quality monitoring and reporting will be enhanced, wastewater will be treated to standards, and hospitals will be encouraged to develop environmental health in accordance with standards.",""]],"55":[[1,"","5.5","Strategic Program on Elevating Paradigms to Stipulate the Future of the Country's Natural Resources and Environment","69.0 million baht · The amount will be used to manage land resources, promote environmentally friendly production and consumption, foster discipline and participation in waste management, raise awareness of desirable environmental behaviors and quality of life concerning climate change, and enhance the efficiency of environmental impact assessments.",""]],"56":[[1,"","5.6","Integrated Program on Management of Water Resources","62620.6 million baht · The amount will be allocated to increase the country's water security through systematic and sustainable water resource management and address drought issues. These can be achieved by securing water supplies for consumption, ensuring water security in production, agriculture, and industry, enhancing water distribution systems, managing floods in communities and economic areas, improving wastewater management, conserving and restoring watershed areas, preventing soil erosion and degradation, and restoring watershed forests through afforestation.",""]],"57":[[1,"","5.7","Strategic Program on Improvement of Water Resource Management Efficiency","36196.5 million baht · The amount will be allocated for the development, restoration, improvement, and repair of the irrigation system and water distribution system. It will also support water management and irrigation works, manage water sources in and out of irrigation areas and in community and public areas, provide aircraft for the Royal Rainmaking project, and efficiently manage information technology for water management.",""]],"58":[[1,"","5.8","Strategic Program on Supporting Creation of Growth on the Environmental-friendly Quality of Life","913.5 million baht · The amount will be used for conserving, preserving, and properly and sustainably utilizing natural resources and the environment; supporting water management; managing information technology for water management; and improving groundwater resources management.",""]],"59":[[1,"","5.9","Fundamental Program on Creation of Growth on the Environmental-friendly Quality of Life","9879.2 million baht · The amount will be allocated for operations relating to the creation of growth on the environmental-friendly quality of life. The actions include supporting water resources, natural resources, pollution, and environment management; supporting greenhouse gases management; and establishing learning and plant conservation centers.",""]],"60":[[1,"","5.10","Program on Public Sector Personnel","17941.9 million baht · The amount will be allocated to ensure efficiency and cost effectiveness in the management of public sector personnel. In addition, there will be development of the government agencies' work system and personnel capacity so they can perform their duties with efficiency, morality and ethics while maintaining work-life balance.",""]],"61":[[1,"","6.1","Strategic Program on Improvement of Public Service Delivery and the Public Sector's Efficiency","29353.7 million baht · The amount will be allocated to improve public service delivery to be simple, convenient, quick, transparent, cost-effective, and accountable. It includes improving monetary and fiscal management, revenue collection, tax systems, fiscal systems, budgeting processes, public debt management, monitoring and evaluation systems, public sector rebalancing, and training public sector personnel to be moral, ethical, competent, knowledgeable, and skillful.",""]],"62":[[1,"","6.2","Integrated Program on Digital Government","3538.9 million baht · The amount will be allocated to promote the transformation of government operations into a digital government and enhance the efficiency of public services. This involves comprehensive use of technology and digital systems, seamless digital public services, citizen-centric service delivery, complete data integration between agencies, electronic public services for citizens and businesses, improved approval and permitting systems, systems for collecting and disclosing government data, and reducing legal constraints to elevate government development toward a fully digital government.",""]],"63":[[1,"","6.3","Integrated Program on Anti-corruption and Misconduct","953.6 million baht · The amount will be allocated to address corruption and misconduct issues by utilizing modern technology in service delivery. It supports corruption prevention and elimination with public participation, promotes transparency and good governance through information disclosure and public monitoring, integrates management and decision-making processes, fosters awareness and values of honesty and integrity in all sectors, and improves laws and their strict and fair enforcement.",""]],"64":[[1,"","6.4","Strategic Program on Developing Laws and the Judicial Process","18666.1 million baht · The amount will be allocated to improve the efficiency of the justice system and foster integrated collaboration among relevant agencies. The program supports fairness in protecting citizens' rights, developing appropriate laws, enforcing laws transparently and efficiently, promoting equitable justice through innovation and digital technology, reducing legal barriers, modernizing outdated laws, developing participatory models in the justice process, protecting rights and freedoms, and enhancing investigation and surveillance systems with clearly defined timelines.",""]],"65":[[1,"","6.5","Strategic Program on Supporting Realignment for Balance and Development of Administrative System of the Public Sector","456660.6 million baht · The amount will be used to support the strategic goal on realignment for balance and development of the administrative system of the public sector by ensuring a work culture focused on results and common interests, responsiveness to people's needs, downsizing the public sector, eliminating corruption, adopting big data technology and digital working processes, opening public participation, encouraging integrity and thrift, enforcing relevant and up-to-date laws, and managing the judicial process to be efficient, fair, and in accordance with the rule of law.",""]],"66":[[1,"","6.6","Fundamental Program on Realignment for Balance and Development of Administrative System of the Public Sector","24789.7 million baht · The amount will be allocated to carry out responsibilities on realigning and developing an administrative system to be efficient and cost effective, allowing public agencies to operate and provide standard services continuously with regard to their authority and laws while personnel, workplaces, equipment and the working environment are maintained in good condition.",""]],"67":[[1,"","6.7","Program on Public Sector Personnel","111536.9 million baht · The amount will be allocated to ensure efficiency and cost effectiveness in the management of public sector personnel. In addition, there will be development of the government agencies' work system and personnel capacity so they can perform their duties with efficiency, morality and ethics while maintaining work-life balance, and the government personnel evaluation system will be enhanced to reflect their potentials in driving the country's goals.",""]],"68":[[1,"","7.1","Program on Attending to Emergencies or Necessities","285056.7 million baht · The amount will be reserved as expenditures to prevent or rectify situations concerning public order and national security, compensate or alleviate serious public disasters, stimulate the economy and strengthen the economic system, and use in the state's urgent necessities, as well as compensate for construction cost to assist construction business operators, with respect to fiscal discipline.",""]],"69":[[1,"","7.2","Program on Management of Public Debt","410253.7 million baht · The amount will be allocated to support the efficient management and repayment of public debt with maximum benefits to the economy.",""]]}});
PVD("thailand_budget_2026",{"docs":["","Table I-4 Budget Allocation Strategy and Program FY 2026"],"s":{"1":[[1,"","1.1","Strategic Program on Strengthening the Nation's Principal Institutions","13436.1 million baht · The amount of 13,436.1 million baht will be allocated to foster loyalty, honesty, and commitment among Thai people to uphold the nation's principal institutions, provide the security to the King and royal family. This includes instilling awareness and appreciation of the nation's principal institutions, reinforcing national identity, incorporating the development of areas knowledge in alignment of the royal initiatives and the Sufficiency Economy Philosophy, along with supporting special royal activities.",""]],"2":[[1,"","1.2","Strategic Program on Maintaining Internal Peace","28609.6 million baht · The amount of 28,609.6 million baht will be allocated to ensure security and safety of citizens in their lives and property. The program focuses on preserving national stability and public order, fostering a sense of unity and promoting harmony among citizens, supporting the operations of Territorial Defense Volunteers and local militia forces, and advancing government policies through village mechanisms.",""]],"3":[[1,"","1.3","Strategic Program on Developing and Strengthening Politics in the Democratic Regime with the Monarchy as Head of State","946.9 million baht · The amount of 946.9 million baht will be allocated to ensure political stability and good governance. Focus will be on promoting public relations for democracy development, and fostering public participation in political process.",""]],"4":[[1,"","1.4","Integrated Program on Mobilization of Problem Rectification of Southern Border Provinces","1473.4 million baht · The amount of 1,473.4 million baht will be allocated to ensure national security, and guarantee the safety of life and property for the people residing in the area, fostering a peaceful coexistence within a multicultural society. The strategy involves a systematically integrated and unified approach to resolving issues and promoting development across all target areas and groups.",""]],"5":[[1,"","1.5","Strategic Program on Management of Problems of Alien Workforce and Human Trafficking","420.7 million baht · The amount of 420.7 million baht will be allocated to promote an integrated approach to preventing and addressing human trafficking. It aims to advance efforts in combating forced labor and human trafficking while ensuring that victims, including children, forced laborers, and vulnerable groups, receive protection and assistance systematically.",""]],"6":[[1,"","1.6","Integrated Program on Prevention, Suppression and Treatment of Drug Addiction","5474.0 million baht · The amount of 5,474.0 million baht will be allocated to protect children, youth, laborers, and at-risk groups from the threats posed by drugs, ensuring that they are not involved with narcotics. Emphasis will be given to establish a systematic mechanism for planning prevention, resolution, and assistance measures for the public.",""]],"7":[[1,"","1.7","Strategic Program on Preventing and Rectifying Problems with Repercussions to the Security","23754.8 million baht · The amount of 23,754.8 million baht will be allocated to address security-related issues to the extent that they do not affect the country's administration and development. The program focuses on maintaining internal stability and public order within the country, securing borders and coastal areas, and safeguarding national maritime interests.",""]],"8":[[1,"","1.8","Strategic Program on Developing National Preparedness System and Disaster Management System","26365.0 million baht · The amount of 26,365.0 million baht will be allocated to build public confidence in emergency and rescue operations, as well as to minimize loss, and ensure safety in the citizens' lives and properties. The program will enhance operational capacity, prepare the equipment and tools for disaster prevention and recovery, and improve the efficiency of early warning systems.",""]],"9":[[1,"","1.9","Strategic Program on Developing National Defense Capacity and Preparedness in Coping with all Forms of Threats","63499.1 million baht · The amount of 63,499.1 million baht will be allocated to ensure that security agencies are better prepared to confront all types of threats. This initiative emphasizes the development of a modern and practical national preparedness framework and actionable plans.",""]],"10":[[1,"","1.10","Strategic Program on Developing a Holistic Security Administration Mechanism","374.6 million baht · The amount of 374.6 million baht will be allocated to enhance the efficiency of security management mechanisms. This program aims to advance the National Security Policies and Plans, ensuring a comprehensive approach to security management at all levels.",""]],"11":[[1,"","1.11","Strategic Program on Promoting International Relations","5391.7 million baht · The amount of 5,391.7 million baht will be allocated to enhance Thailand's ability to respond effectively to external challenges. This program aims to establish unity in foreign affairs, align the nation's efforts with international standards, and preserve national interests.",""]],"12":[[1,"","1.12","Strategic Program on Supporting National Security","14.3 million baht · The amount of 14.3 million baht will be allocated to support the strategic goal of national security. This initiative emphasizes managing the nation's environment to maintain security, safety, independence, sovereignty, and public order.",""]],"13":[[1,"","1.13","Fundamental Program on National Security","38247.2 million baht · The amount of 38,247.2 million baht will be allocated to ensure the efficient and cost-effective execution of national security missions. This program aims to enable government agencies to perform their duties and provide continuous services in accordance with their legal mandate and standards.",""]],"14":[[1,"","1.14","Program on Public Sector Personnel","205900.2 million baht · The amount of 205,900.2 million baht will be allocated to ensure efficiency and cost effectiveness in the management of public sector personnel. In addition, there will be development of the government agencies' work system and personnel competencies in order to perform their duties with efficiency, morality, and ethics while maintaining their work-life balance.",""]],"15":[[1,"","2.1","Strategic Program on Value Creation Agriculture","34917.4 million baht · The amount of 34,917.4 million baht will be allocated to increase the growth of the agricultural sector's GDP, enhance productivity, and transform agricultural output into high-value downstream products. This initiative emphasizes utilizing advanced technologies to strengthen and sustain agricultural resources.",""]],"16":[[1,"","2.2","Integrated Program on Development of Future Industries and Services","5884.2 million baht · The amount of 5,884.2 million baht will be allocated to increase the growth rate of the industrial and service sector's GDP and improve productivity within these sectors. This initiative focuses on promoting bioindustry, advancing entrepreneurs and skilled workers in high-tech fields, and fostering the comprehensive development of medical industries and services.",""]],"17":[[1,"","2.3","Strategic Program on Promoting and Developing Tourism Potential","2534.1 million baht · The amount of 2,534.1 million baht will be allocated to enhance Thailand's tourism competitiveness and increase the tourism sector's contribution to the GDP. This program aims to elevate safety standards and mitigate impacts from tourism activities across all dimensions.",""]],"18":[[1,"","2.4","Integrated Program on Creating Income from Tourism","5497.3 million baht · The amount of 5,497.3 million baht will be allocated to increase the contribution of tourism sector to the GDP and improve Thailand's tourism competitiveness. The initiative focuses on distributing tourism activities across different regions and channeling income towards local communities.",""]],"19":[[1,"","2.5","Strategic Program on Area Development and Smart Livable City","11371.3 million baht · The amount of 11,371.3 million baht will be allocated to enhance Thailand's competitiveness and create centers of economic and social prosperity across all regions of the country. This will be achieved by developing transportation infrastructure, communication systems, and energy systems using advanced digital technology.",""]],"20":[[1,"","2.6","Strategic Program on Development of Transport and Logistics System","216193.4 million baht · The amount of 216,193.4 million baht will be allocated to ensure Thailand possesses an efficient transportation and logistics system. The program aims to develop, maintain, and oversee transportation infrastructure across various modes including railways, waterways, roads, aviation, and associated facilities.",""]],"21":[[1,"","2.7","Strategic Program on Development of Energy Security","1844.4 million baht · The amount of 1,844.4 million baht will be allocated to enable Thailand to have energy security and improve efficiency in the country's energy consumption. This program aims to promote and develop the surrounding factors necessary for energy procurement while advancing the infrastructure related to energy systems to achieve appropriate levels of security.",""]],"22":[[1,"","2.8","Strategic Program on Development of Digital Economy and Society","1545.4 million baht · The amount of 1,545.4 million baht will be allocated to increase the contribution of digital businesses to the GDP and foster the expansion of the domestic digital economy. The program focuses on the development of digital infrastructure, including high-quality, reliable, and secure broadband networks that are accessible nationwide.",""]],"23":[[1,"","2.9","Strategic Program on Supporting Strong and Competitive Small and Medium-sized Enterprises","4141.2 million baht · The amount of 4,141.2 million baht will be allocated to empower entrepreneurs at all levels to become modern entrepreneurs who play a significant role in the economic system. This initiative aims to equip small and medium-sized enterprises and community entrepreneurs with the knowledge and skills necessary to establish clear identities.",""]],"24":[[1,"","2.10","Strategic Program on Driving Soft Power Policy","3928.4 million baht · The amount of 3,928.4 million baht will be allocated to advance Thailand's soft power industry, ensuring sustained growth while fostering job creation, income generation, and entrepreneurial development for modern business leaders within the economic system. This initiative emphasizes the promotion and development of entrepreneurs capable of driving businesses through creativity and cultural capital.",""]],"25":[[1,"","2.11","Strategic Program on Development of Special Economic Zones","470.2 million baht · The amount of 470.2 million baht will be allocated to promote the development of special economic zones as centers for economic and social prosperity. This initiative focuses on enhancing the areas' infrastructure including transportation, social development, environment, and education.",""]],"26":[[1,"","2.12","Integrated Program on Development of the Eastern Economic Corridor","8208.6 million baht · The amount of 8,208.6 million baht will be allocated to promote the growth of the gross regional product and increase investment in the Eastern Economic Corridor. The program encourages the development of modern, environmentally friendly economic activities to enhance the country's competitiveness.",""]],"27":[[1,"","2.13","Strategic Program on Research and Innovation Development","19728.3 million baht · The amount of 19,728.3 million baht will be allocated to enhance the competitiveness of technological and scientific infrastructure within the country, aiming to increase the value of investment in research and innovation to the GDP. The program emphasizes research and innovation that align with the country's needs while encouraging the private sector to play an active role.",""]],"28":[[1,"","2.14","Strategic Program on Supporting the Development of Competitiveness","21744.0 million baht · The amount of 21,744.0 million baht will be allocated to support the strategic goal of developing the country's competitiveness to make Thailand a developed country with stable and sustainable economic growth. This goal can be achieved by elevating the country's potential in various dimensions including the economy, identity, culture, tradition, way of life, natural resources, as well as leveraging the country's comparative advantages in other areas.",""]],"29":[[1,"","2.15","Fundamental Program on the Development of Competitiveness","17644.2 million baht · The amount of 17,644.2 million baht will be allocated to ensure the efficient and cost-effective execution of competitiveness enhancement missions. This program aims to enable government agencies to perform their duties and provide continuous services in accordance with their legal mandate and standards.",""]],"30":[[1,"","2.16","Program on Public Sector Personnel","43682.5 million baht · The amount of 43,682.5 million baht will be allocated to ensure efficiency and cost effectiveness in the management of public sector personnel. In addition, there will be development of the government agencies' work system and personnel capacity in order to perform their duties with efficiency, morality, and ethics while maintaining their work-life balance.",""]],"31":[[1,"","3.1","Strategic Program on Realignment of Value and Culture","3396.6 million baht · The amount of 3,396.6 million baht will be allocated to instill in citizens good morals, ethics, values, and culture, fostering a public-mindedness and social responsibility. This initiative focuses on integrating religious principles and the philosophy of Sufficiency Economy into everyday life.",""]],"32":[[1,"","3.2","Strategic Program on Development of Human Potentials on a Life-Long Basis","38317.2 million baht · The amount of 38,317.2 million baht will be allocated to ensure the comprehensive development of individuals across all age groups, fostering strong and stable families and communities. This initiative includes the promotion and development of children, starting from pregnancy through early childhood, to ensure their well-being and appropriate developmental milestones.",""]],"33":[[1,"","3.3","Strategic Program on Development of Education and Learning Quality","35054.7 million baht · The amount of 35,054.7 million baht will be allocated to ensure that Thai people receive high quality education that meets international standards and equips them with essential skills for adapting to the changes of the 21st century. This program focuses on curriculum development, restructuring learning approaches, and enhancing teaching methodologies.",""]],"34":[[1,"","3.4","Strategic Program on Good Public Health Promotion","71087.3 million baht · The amount of 71,087.3 million baht will be allocated to enhance the physical and mental well-being of the Thai people. This initiative aims to ensure access to standardized, efficient, and universally available public health services.",""]],"35":[[1,"","3.5","Strategic Program on Enhancing Sports Potentials","3824.7 million baht · The amount of 3,824.7 million baht will be allocated to promote good health and awareness of the benefits of exercise and sports. This program aims to encourage people of all age groups to engage in regular physical activities, sports, and recreational activities.",""]],"36":[[1,"","3.6","Strategic Program on Supporting Human Potentials Development and Reinforcement","424.1 million baht · The amount of 424.1 million baht will be allocated to support the strategic goal of developing and reinforcing human resource potential. This initiative aims to empower Thai individuals across all age groups to become skilled, virtuous, and of high quality, fostering a love for learning and ensuring equitable access to a comprehensive and high-standard education system.",""]],"37":[[1,"","3.7","Fundamental Program on Human Potentials Development and Reinforcement","23057.8 million baht · The amount of 23,057.8 million baht will be allocated to efficiently carry out missions and legal mandates in human resource development. This program aims to ensure individuals across all age groups have access to high-quality education and improved living standards.",""]],"38":[[1,"","3.8","Program on Public Sector Personnel","429643.3 million baht · The amount of 429,643.3 million baht will be allocated to ensure efficiency and cost effectiveness in the management of public sector personnel. In addition, there will be development of the government agencies' work system and personnel capacity in order to perform their duties with efficiency, morality, and ethics while maintaining their work-life balance.",""]],"39":[[1,"","4.1","Strategic Program on Social Empowerment","7334.3 million baht · The amount of 7,334.3 million baht will be allocated to promote community empowerment as a social force and increase participation from all sectors in social development. This program supports initiatives aimed at strengthening family bonds, eliminating domestic violence, and encouraging the younger generation to contribute to public development and benefit.",""]],"40":[[1,"","4.2","Strategic Program on Decentralization to the Local Administrative Organizations","377960.2 million baht · The amount of 377,960.2 million baht will be allocated to align with the Determining Plans and Process of Decentralization to Local Government Organization Act B.E. 2542 and its amendments. This program aims to promote decentralization of authority to local administrative organizations, enabling them to achieve self-sufficiency in all dimensions.",""]],"41":[[1,"","4.3","Strategic Program on Promoting Integrated Development of Provinces and Clusters of Provinces","26330.8 million baht · The amount of 26,330.8 million baht will be allocated to promote the integrated development of provinces and provincial clusters. The initiative aims to position provinces as centers of economic, social, and technological advancement while emphasizing the active participation of local citizens in shaping the developmental direction of their areas.",""]],"42":[[1,"","4.4","Integrated Program on Preparedness to Accommodate the Aging Society","784.7 million baht · The amount of 784.7 million baht will be allocated to enhance preparedness for individuals transitioning into an aging society with quality and security across all dimensions. This initiative aims to improve the quality of life for the elderly by promoting knowledge in economics, social aspects, and health, as well as developing environments that support the living conditions of the elderly.",""]],"43":[[1,"","4.5","Strategic Program on Development and Promotion of Local Economy","2072.3 million baht · The amount of 2,072.3 million baht will be allocated to ensure continuous and appropriately distributed income growth for farmers, households, communities, and low-income individuals. The program aims to enhance knowledge and essential skills for increasing the workforce's capacity within the grassroots economy.",""]],"44":[[1,"","4.6","Strategic Program on Land and Soil Resource Management","1847.7 million baht · The amount of 1,847.7 million baht will be allocated to develop mechanisms for the utilization of public land for national land and soil resource management. This initiative supports the development of mechanism to act as land trustees from private owners and circulate the land for the benefit of low-income individuals.",""]],"45":[[1,"","4.7","Strategic Program on Creating Social Security","400753.5 million baht · The amount of 400,753.5 million baht will be allocated to ensure citizens' convenient access to basic medical services close to their residence. Key initiatives include enhancing the benefits of the universal health coverage, allowing eligible individuals to receive comprehensive, high-quality, and standardized medical and public health services.",""]],"46":[[1,"","4.8","Strategic Program on Creating Equality in Education","93099.4 million baht · The amount of 93,099.4 million baht will be allocated to ensure equitable access to quality and standard education. This program aims to guarantee basic education rights for all, both formal and nonformal systems, by supporting expenses related to educational management from kindergarten through to the completion of basic education.",""]],"47":[[1,"","4.9","Strategic Program on Targeted Measures to Solve Group-Specific Problems","13360.7 million baht · The amount of 13,360.7 million baht will be allocated to ensure that individuals of all ages, particularly the underprivileged and vulnerable groups, have access to opportunities, adequate social protection, and welfare tailored to their living conditions. This initiative seeks to expand systems and mechanisms to provide assistance to special target groups, including children, youth, women, the elderly, persons with disabilities, victims of violence, and human trafficking survivors.",""]],"48":[[1,"","4.10","Strategic Program on Supporting Creation of Social Opportunities and Equality","8440.0 million baht · The amount of 8,440.0 million baht will be allocated to sustainably enhance the quality of life for low-income individuals and farmers. The program provides support for land allocation, allowing individuals to own agricultural land for farming and residential purposes, thereby addressing issues of land rights loss.",""]],"49":[[1,"","4.11","Fundamental Program on Creating Social Opportunities and Equality","643.5 million baht · The amount of 643.5 million baht will be allocated to support the Creation of Social Opportunity and Equity strategy. The initiative intends to enhance public administration efficiency, ensuring high performance and adaptability in the digital era.",""]],"50":[[1,"","4.12","Program on Public Sector Personnel","8672.8 million baht · The amount of 8,672.8 million baht will be allocated to ensure efficiency and cost effectiveness in the management of public sector personnel. In addition, there will be development of the government agencies' work systems and personnel capacity in order to perform their duties with efficiency, morality, and ethics while maintaining their work-life balance.",""]],"51":[[1,"","5.1","Strategic Program on Creation of Sustainable Growth with Regard to Conservation, Rehabilitation and Prevention of Natural Resources Destruction","7370.5 million baht · The amount of 7,370.5 million baht will be allocated to conserve and restore biodiversity through the development of mechanisms and measures aimed at preservation, protection, risk mitigation, restoration, and sustainable utilization of biodiversity. Efforts will emphasize the expansion of green spaces of all types, the comprehensive cultivation of economic timber, and the enhancement of mangrove forest conservation and restoration.",""]],"52":[[1,"","5.2","Strategic Program on Creation of Sustainable Growth of Marine Economic Society","891.2 million baht · The amount of 891.2 million baht will be allocated to ensure the protection, restoration, and sustainable development of marine and coastal resources. This program emphasizes measures to prevent coastal erosion, manage seawater quality, and reduce waste and pollutants entering the sea.",""]],"53":[[1,"","5.3","Strategic Program on Coping with Repercussions from Climate Change","2367.3 million baht · The amount of 2,367.3 million baht will be allocated to enable the country to reduce greenhouse gas emissions and mitigate the impacts of natural disasters. The program aims to enhance adaptive capacity while addressing the effects of climate change and natural disasters.",""]],"54":[[1,"","5.4","Strategic Program on Dealing with Pollution and the Environment","1152.6 million baht · The amount of 1,152.6 million baht will be allocated to ensure that the country will have effective and quality environmental management, fostering better living standards for the people. This strategy aims to systematically and efficiently address the issue of disposing of industrial waste and all types of garbage, prevent, resolve, and manage pollution from its sources, and promote land management practices that discourage agricultural burning.",""]],"55":[[1,"","5.5","Strategic Program on Elevating Paradigms to Stipulate the Future of the Country's Natural Resources and Environment","77.0 million baht · The amount of 77.0 million baht will be allocated to manage soil resources, promote environmentally friendly production and consumption, enhance discipline and participation in waste management, and raise awareness regarding desirable environmental behaviors and improved quality of life. This program also seeks to address climate change and improve the efficiency of environmental impact assessments.",""]],"56":[[1,"","5.6","Integrated Program on Management of Water Resources","63401.1 million baht · The amount of 63,401.1 million baht will be allocated to enhance the country's water security through systematic and sustainable water resource management. It seeks to address drought issues by ensuring the availability of water supplies for consumption, including the provision of reserve water sources for water supply systems.",""]],"57":[[1,"","5.7","Strategic Program on Improvement of Water Resource Management Efficiency","43652.3 million baht · The amount of 43,652.3 million baht will be allocated to develop, restore, improve, and repair irrigation systems and water distribution networks. The program supports the management of water resources and irrigation projects, encompassing both areas within and outside irrigation zones, as well as community and public water sources.",""]],"58":[[1,"","5.8","Strategic Program on Supporting Creation of Growth on the Environmental-friendly Quality of Life","213.0 million baht · The amount of 213.0 million baht will be allocated to conserve, preserve, and utilize natural resources and the environment in a balanced and sustainable manner. It also supports water resource management, information technology management for resource administration, and enhances the capacity for groundwater resource management.",""]],"59":[[1,"","5.9","Fundamental Program on Creation of Growth on the Environmental-friendly Quality of Life","9801.7 million baht · The amount of 9,801.7 million baht will be allocated for the operation relating to the creation of growth on the environmental-friendly quality of life. This includes supporting the management of water resources, natural resources, pollution, and the environment.",""]],"60":[[1,"","5.10","Program on Public Sector Personnel","17731.3 million baht · The amount of 17,731.3 million baht will be allocated to ensure efficiency and cost effectiveness in the management of public sector personnel. In addition, there will be development of the government agencies' work system and personnel capacity in order to perform their duties with efficiency, morality and ethics while maintaining their work-life balance.",""]],"61":[[1,"","6.1","Strategic Program on Improvement of Public Service Delivery and the Public Sector's Efficiency","29879.9 million baht · The amount of 29,879.9 million baht will be allocated to improve public services delivery, ensuring that it is simple, convenient, quick, transparent, cost-effective, and accountable. This program includes the financial and fiscal administration to enhance efficiency in revenue collection, expand the tax base, and modernize the tax system to align with the country's economic circumstances.",""]],"62":[[1,"","6.2","Integrated Program on Digital Government","6856.7 million baht · The amount of 6,856.7 million baht will be allocated to enhancing government services through the efficient application of digital technology. This initiative adopts a citizen-centric approach to deliver valuable services that meet international standards.",""]],"63":[[1,"","6.3","Integrated Program on Anti-corruption and Misconduct","943.3 million baht · The amount of 943.3 million baht will be allocated to mitigate corruption issues within Thai society through fostering awareness and instilling values in all sectors about integrity, morality, and ethics. This initiative aims to embed good governance within organizational management and rigorously and fairly improve and enforce laws.",""]],"64":[[1,"","6.4","Strategic Program on Developing Laws and the Judicial Process","17568.0 million baht · The amount of 17,568.0 million baht will be allocated to develop laws, regulations, rules, and measures to be appropriate and consistent with the country's context, changes, and conducive to the country's development. This includes reviewing the necessity and appropriateness of existing laws, reducing legal constraints, modernizing, and repealing unnecessary or obstructive laws.",""]],"65":[[1,"","6.5","Strategic Program on Supporting Realignment for Balance and Development of Administrative System of the Public Sector","408313.9 million baht · The amount of 408,313.9 million baht will be allocated to support the strategic goal on rebalancing and developing of the public administration system, fostering a government culture that prioritizes effectiveness and the collective benefit. The program focuses on making public service responding promptly, transparently, and efficiently to public needs, while ensuring a streamlined and adaptable public sector that can swiftly adjust to evolving circumstances.",""]],"66":[[1,"","6.6","Fundamental Program on Realignment for Balance and Development of Administrative System of the Public Sector","25386.5 million baht · The amount of 25,386.5 million baht will be allocated to ensure efficiency and cost-effectiveness in achieving balanced development and administrative improvements within the public sector. This will enable government agencies to operate and deliver services continuously in accordance with their legal mandates and standards, while personnel, workplaces, equipment and the working environment will be maintained in good condition.",""]],"67":[[1,"","6.7","Program on Public Sector Personnel","115280.1 million baht · The amount of 115,280.1 million baht will be allocated to ensure efficiency and cost effectiveness in the management of public sector personnel. In addition, there will be development of the government agencies' work system and personnel capacity in order to perform their duties with efficiency, morality and ethics while maintaining their work-life balance.",""]],"68":[[1,"","7.1","Program on Attending to Emergencies or Necessities","124960.0 million baht · The amount of 124,960.0 million baht will be reserved as expenditures to prevent or rectify situations concerning public order and national security, compensate or alleviate from serious public disasters, stimulate the economy and strengthen the economic system, and use in the state's urgent necessities, as well as compensate for construction cost to assist construction business operators, with respect to the fiscal discipline.",""]],"69":[[1,"","7.2","Program on Management of Public Debt","421864.4 million baht · The amount of 421,864.4 million baht will be allocated to support the efficient management and repayment of public debt with maximum benefits to the economy.",""]],"70":[[1,"","7.3","Program on Expenditures for Replenishment of Treasury Account Balance","123541.1 million baht · The amount of 123,541.1 million baht will be allocated to reimburse the expenditures withdrawn from the treasury account in accordance with the Treasury Account Act of B.E. 2491 and its amendments.",""]]}});